nt":"Process an unsubscribe from your own page"},"1614":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-36","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#one-click-unsubscribe-rfc-8058","content":"One-click unsubscribe (RFC 8058)"},"1615":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-37","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#related","content":"Related"},"1616":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-38","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#subscriptions-api","content":"The Subscriptions API is the one place to change who receives which mail. Use it from your own application to build newsletter signups, a preference page inside your product, or server-side opt-outs. Every call applies the same rules as NorthRelay's hosted forms, unsubscribe links and preference centre, and fires the same webhooks."},"1617":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-39","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#subscriptions-api","content":"For a walkthrough of how the pieces fit together, see the Mailing Lists guide."},"1618":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-40","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"| Term     | What it is                                                              | Managed with      |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| **List** | An audience you send campaigns to. A contact is either a member or not. | `/contacts/lists` |","table":"table-0"},"1619":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-41","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"| Term      | What it is                                                                                                                                                                           | Managed with          |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------- |\n| **Topic** | A category of mail a recipient can opt out of (for example \"Product updates\"). Stored as a suppression group. A member row in a topic means the address **opted out** of that topic. | `/suppression-groups` |","table":"table-0"},"1620":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-42","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"| Term                   | What it is                                                                                                                                                   | Managed with |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------ |\n| **Global unsubscribe** | The recipient wants no marketing mail at all. The contact status becomes `UNSUBSCRIBED` and an account-level suppression with reason `Unsubscribe` is added. | This API     |","table":"table-0"},"1621":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-43","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Rules the API enforces for you:"},"1622":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-44","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Subscribing to a topic means removing the recipient's opt-out for it. Opting out of a topic also removes the recipient from every list tagged with that topic."},"1623":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-45","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Unsubscribing from a list keeps the membership history (the membership is marked removed). Removing a member as the list owner deletes it (see list members)."},"1624":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-46","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Someone who unsubscribed is never re-added silently. You must pass `\"resubscribe\": true`, and you should only do so after fresh consent."},"1625":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-47","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Bounce, complaint and manual suppressions are never lifted by a subscribe call."},"1626":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-48","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Contacts with status `COMPLAINED` or `CLEANED` cannot be resubscribed."},"1627":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-49","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#authentication-and-scopes","content":"All endpoints in the first part of this page take an API key: `Authorization: Bearer nr_live_...`. Restricted keys need these scopes:"},"1628":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-50","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#authentication-and-scopes","content":"| Endpoint                     | Scope           |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------- |\n| `GET /subscriptions/{email}` | `contacts:read` |","table":"table-1"},"1629":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-51","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#authentication-and-scopes","content":"| Endpoint                                                                                                                                    | Scope            |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `POST /subscriptions`, `POST /subscriptions/unsubscribe`, `PATCH /subscriptions/{email}`, `POST /subscriptions/{email}/resend-confirmation` | `contacts:write` |","table":"table-1"},"1630":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-52","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#authentication-and-scopes","content":"A key without the scope receives `403 SCOPE_INSUFFICIENT`; a missing or invalid key receives `401`."},"1631":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-53","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#authentication-and-scopes","content":"The public endpoints for unsubscribe pages you host yourself (`POST /unsubscribe`, `POST /unsubscribe/one-click`) take the signed token from the unsubscribe link instead of an API key. See Unsubscribe links."},"1632":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-54","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#response-format","content":"Successful responses use the standard envelope:"},"1633":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-55","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#response-format","content":"Errors include the fix:"},"1634":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-56","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#response-format","content":"Validation errors use code `VALIDATION_ERROR` and name the offending field in `error.context.field`."},"1635":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-57","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#subscribe","content":"Create or update a contact, add it to lists, opt it into topics and record consent. With `doubleOptIn: true` NorthRelay emails a confirmation link and the contact stays `PENDING` until the recipient clicks it."},"1636":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-58","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#subscribe","content":"Returns `201` when the contact was created, `200` when it already existed. Repeating the same call is safe: nothing is added twice."},"1637":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-59","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"Unknown fields are rejected."},"1638":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-60","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field   | Type   | Required | Description                                                    |\n| ------- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `email` | string | Yes      | Recipient address. Trimmed and lowercased. Max 254 characters. |","table":"table-2"},"1639":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-61","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field       | Type   | Required | Description        |\n| ----------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `firstName` | string | No       | Max 100 characters |","table":"table-2"},"1640":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-62","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field      | Type   | Required | Description        |\n| ---------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `lastName` | string | No       | Max 100 characters |","table":"table-2"},"1641":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-63","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field   | Type   | Required | Description       |\n| ------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------- |\n| `phone` | string | No       | Max 40 characters |","table":"table-2"},"1642":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-64","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field     | Type     | Required | Description                          |\n| --------- | -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `listIds` | string[] | No       | Lists to add the contact to (max 50) |","table":"table-2"},"1643":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-65","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field      | Type     | Required | Description                                                      |\n| ---------- | -------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `topicIds` | string[] | No       | Topics to opt the contact into, i.e. remove any opt-out (max 50) |","table":"table-2"},"1644":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-66","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field  | Type     | Required | Description                                |\n| ------ | -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `tags` | string[] | No       | Tags to add (max 50, each 1–50 characters) |","table":"table-2"},"1645":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-67","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field          | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                |\n| -------------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `customFields` | object | No       | String key/value pairs stored as custom fields (keys max 100, values max 1,000 characters) |","table":"table-2"},"1646":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-68","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field      | Type   | Required | Description                                                       |\n| ---------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `metadata` | object | No       | Arbitrary JSON stored on the contact (replaces existing metadata) |","table":"table-2"},"1647":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-69","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field         | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                                               |\n| ------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `doubleOptIn` | boolean | No       | Send a confirmation email and keep the contact `PENDING` until confirmed. Ignored for a contact that is already `ACTIVE`. |","table":"table-2"},"1648":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-70","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field                    | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------ | ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `confirmationTemplateId` | string | No       | One of your templates to use for the confirmation email. It can use `{{confirm_url}}`, `{{first_name}}`, `{{last_name}}` and `{{email}}`. Defaults to NorthRelay's confirmation template with your brand theme. |","table":"table-2"},"1649":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-71","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field         | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                   |\n| ------------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `redirectUrl` | string | No       | `https://` URL the recipient is sent to after confirming. Without it they see a NorthRelay confirmation page. |","table":"table-2"},"1650":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-72","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field         | Type    | Required | Description                                                                             |\n| ------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resubscribe` | boolean | No       | Required to re-add someone who previously unsubscribed. Only use it with fresh consent. |","table":"table-2"},"1651":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-73","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body","content":"| Field     | Type   | Required | Description                                                |\n| --------- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `consent` | object | No       | Consent evidence: `{ ip?, userAgent?, text? }`. See below. |","table":"table-2"},"1652":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-74","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#consent-evidence","content":"NorthRelay stores the consent source (`api` for this endpoint), the time, and whatever you pass in `consent`:"},"1653":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-75","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#consent-evidence","content":"| Field        | Type   | Description                                                                                                           |\n| ------------ | ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `consent.ip` | string | The subscriber's IP address. Pass it from your server: NorthRelay only sees your server's address. Max 64 characters. |","table":"table-3"},"1654":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-76","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#consent-evidence","content":"| Field               | Type   | Description                                                |\n| ------------------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `consent.userAgent` | string | The subscriber's browser user agent. Max 1,024 characters. |","table":"table-3"},"1655":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-77","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#consent-evidence","content":"| Field          | Type   | Description                                                                                        |\n| -------------- | ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `consent.text` | string | The exact wording the subscriber agreed to (for example the checkbox label). Max 2,000 characters. |","table":"table-3"},"1656":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-78","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#consent-evidence","content":"Together these are the record of express consent that CASL (Canada) and GDPR (EU) expect you to be able to produce. Consent is recorded when the contact is created, when it is resubscribed, or when it had no consent record yet; a repeat subscribe does not overwrite earlier evidence. Read it back with Get subscription status."},"1657":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-79","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"| Field       | Description      |\n| ----------- | ---------------- |\n| `contactId` | The contact's id |","table":"table-4"},"1658":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-80","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"| Field    | Description                                                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `ACTIVE`, or `PENDING` while a double opt-in is outstanding |","table":"table-4"},"1659":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-81","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"| Field     | Description                               |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `created` | `true` when this call created the contact |","table":"table-4"},"1660":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-82","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"| Field     | Description             |\n| --------- | ----------------------- |\n| `listIds` | The lists you asked for |","table":"table-4"},"1661":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-83","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"| Field            | Description                                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `addedToListIds` | The lists the contact was actually added to by this call (empty when it was already a member) |","table":"table-4"},"1662":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-84","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"| Field      | Description              |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ |\n| `topicIds` | The topics you asked for |","table":"table-4"},"1663":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-85","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"| Field                  | Description                                                                    |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `requiresConfirmation` | `true` when a confirmation email is required before the contact becomes active |","table":"table-4"},"1664":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-86","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"| Field              | Description                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `confirmationSent` | `true` when the confirmation email was sent. It is `false` if platform sending is temporarily paused; retry later with Resend confirmation. |","table":"table-4"},"1665":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-87","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-201","content":"Webhooks: `contact.subscribed` (with `source: \"API\"`), plus one `list.member_added` per list in `addedToListIds`."},"1666":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-88","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#double-opt-in-flow","content":"Your app calls `POST /subscriptions` with `doubleOptIn: true`. The contact is `PENDING`."},"1667":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-89","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#double-opt-in-flow","content":"The recipient receives a confirmation email with a link to `https://app.northrelay.ca/c/<token>`. The link is valid for 7 days."},"1668":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-90","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#double-opt-in-flow","content":"When they click it, the contact becomes `ACTIVE`, a `contact.confirmed` webhook fires, and the recipient is redirected to your `redirectUrl` (or shown a confirmation page)."},"1669":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-91","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#double-opt-in-flow","content":"List memberships and topic opt-ins are applied immediately, so the contact appears in the list, with status `PENDING`, as soon as you subscribe it. Campaigns skip `PENDING` contacts until they confirm."},"1670":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-92","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors","content":"| Code               | Status | When                                                                       | Fix                                              |\n| ------------------ | ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400    | Missing or invalid field, unknown field, or a non-`https://` `redirectUrl` | Correct the field named in `error.context.field` |","table":"table-5"},"1671":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-93","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors","content":"| Code                      | Status | When                                             | Fix                                      |\n| ------------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `FREE_TIER_CONTACT_LIMIT` | 403    | A Free account already holds 100 active contacts | Upgrade at `/dashboard/settings/billing` |","table":"table-5"},"1672":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-94","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors","content":"| Code             | Status | When                                             | Fix                                            |\n| ---------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `LIST_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | A `listIds` entry does not exist in your account | Check the id with `GET /api/v1/contacts/lists` |","table":"table-5"},"1673":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-95","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors","content":"| Code              | Status | When                                              | Fix                                                |\n| ----------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `TOPIC_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | A `topicIds` entry does not exist in your account | Check the id with `GET /api/v1/suppression-groups` |","table":"table-5"},"1674":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-96","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors","content":"| Code                     | Status | When                                                                                                                         | Fix                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------ | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `RECIPIENT_UNSUBSCRIBED` | 409    | The address unsubscribed (contact `UNSUBSCRIBED`, or an `Unsubscribe` or `Manual` suppression) and `resubscribe` was not set | Pass `\"resubscribe\": true` only with fresh consent, ideally with `\"doubleOptIn\": true` |","table":"table-5"},"1675":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-97","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors","content":"| Code                   | Status | When                                                                                                               | Fix                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `RECIPIENT_SUPPRESSED` | 409    | The address hard-bounced or complained, or you passed `resubscribe` for an address on your manual suppression list | Cannot be overridden by this API. Remove the suppression with `DELETE /api/v1/suppressions/{email}` only if you have confirmed the address is valid and wants your mail |","table":"table-5"},"1676":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-98","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors","content":"| Code              | Status | When                                              | Fix                                                                  |\n| ----------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CONTACT_BLOCKED` | 409    | The contact's status is `COMPLAINED` or `CLEANED` | Delete the contact and only re-add it with fresh, documented consent |","table":"table-5"},"1677":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-99","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#sdk","content":"TypeScript (`@northrelay/sdk` 1.9.0). Methods return the response envelope, so the result is in `data`. Errors are thrown as `NorthRelayError` with `code` and `fixAction`; `isSubscriptionError(error, code?)` narrows them:"},"1678":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-100","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#sdk","content":"Python (`northrelay` 1.9.0, async). The email is positional, the rest are keyword arguments; the result is a `SubscribeResult` model with snake_case attributes. A 409 raises `NorthRelayError` with the API code in `error.details[\"code\"]`:"},"1679":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-101","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#unsubscribe","content":"Opt an address out from your own server, for example when a user switches off a newsletter in your product's settings."},"1680":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-102","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"| Field   | Type   | Required | Description       |\n| ------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------- |\n| `email` | string | Yes      | Recipient address |","table":"table-6"},"1681":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-103","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"| Field   | Type   | Required | Description                        |\n| ------- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `scope` | string | No       | `all` (default), `list` or `topic` |","table":"table-6"},"1682":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-104","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"| Field    | Type   | Required               | Description       |\n| -------- | ------ | ---------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `listId` | string | When `scope` is `list` | The list to leave |","table":"table-6"},"1683":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-105","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"| Field     | Type   | Required                | Description             |\n| --------- | ------ | ----------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `topicId` | string | When `scope` is `topic` | The topic to opt out of |","table":"table-6"},"1684":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-106","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                        |\n| -------- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `reason` | string | No       | Free text, max 500 characters. Stored on the contact for `scope: all` and included in the webhook. |","table":"table-6"},"1685":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-107","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"What each scope does:"},"1686":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-108","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"| Scope | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `all` | Contact status becomes `UNSUBSCRIBED` and an account-level suppression with reason `Unsubscribe` is added. Works even when the address is not a contact. An existing `Bounce`, `Complaint` or `Manual` suppression is kept. |","table":"table-7"},"1687":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-109","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"| Scope  | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `list` | The contact leaves that list and no longer receives campaigns sent to it. The membership is marked removed so the history stays visible. No effect when the address is not a contact. |","table":"table-7"},"1688":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-110","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-1","content":"| Scope   | Effect                                                                                                                           |\n| ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `topic` | The address is opted out of that topic and removed from every list tagged with it. Works even when the address is not a contact. |","table":"table-7"},"1689":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-111","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response","content":"`changed` is `false` when the address was already opted out, so the call is safe to repeat. `contactId` is `null` when the address is not a contact. A `contact.unsubscribed` webhook (with `method: \"api\"`) fires only when something changed, plus `list.member_removed` for each list the contact left."},"1690":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-112","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-1","content":"| Code               | Status | When                                                                        | Fix                             |\n| ------------------ | ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400    | Invalid email, unknown field, or `listId` / `topicId` missing for its scope | Add the id that matches `scope` |","table":"table-8"},"1691":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-113","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-1","content":"| Code             | Status | When                            | Fix                                            |\n| ---------------- | ------ | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `LIST_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | `listId` is not in your account | Check the id with `GET /api/v1/contacts/lists` |","table":"table-8"},"1692":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-114","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-1","content":"| Code              | Status | When                             | Fix                                                |\n| ----------------- | ------ | -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `TOPIC_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | `topicId` is not in your account | Check the id with `GET /api/v1/suppression-groups` |","table":"table-8"},"1693":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-115","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#get-subscription-status","content":"Everything you need to render a preference page: the contact and its consent evidence, any account-level suppression, a pending double opt-in, every list membership (current and past) and every topic with a `subscribed` flag."},"1694":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-116","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#get-subscription-status","content":"URL-encode the address once (`jane%2Bnews%40example.com` for `jane+news@example.com`); do not double-encode it. An address that is not a contact still returns `200` with `contact: null`, so you can show topic choices before someone subscribes."},"1695":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-117","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-1","content":"| Field     | Description                                                                                                                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contact` | `null` when the address is not a contact. `status` is one of `PENDING`, `ACTIVE`, `UNSUBSCRIBED`, `BOUNCED`, `COMPLAINED`, `CLEANED`. |","table":"table-9"},"1696":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-118","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-1","content":"| Field             | Description                                                                                                                                        |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contact.consent` | Consent evidence: `source` (for example `api`, `form`, `import`, `preference_center`), `at`, `ip`, `userAgent`, `text`. Any of them may be `null`. |","table":"table-9"},"1697":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-119","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-1","content":"| Field         | Description                                                                                                             |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `suppression` | Account-level suppression `{ reason, since }` (`reason` is `Bounce`, `Complaint`, `Unsubscribe` or `Manual`), or `null` |","table":"table-9"},"1698":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-120","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-1","content":"| Field                 | Description                                                                                                               |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `unsubscribedFromAll` | `true` when the contact is `UNSUBSCRIBED` or any account-level suppression exists. No marketing mail reaches the address. |","table":"table-9"},"1699":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-121","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-1","content":"| Field                 | Description                                                       |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pendingConfirmation` | `{ expiresAt }` while a double opt-in is outstanding, else `null` |","table":"table-9"},"1700":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-122","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-1","content":"| Field   | Description                                                                                                                 |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lists` | Every list the contact has been a member of, newest first. `subscribed` is `false` (with `removedAt`) after an unsubscribe. |","table":"table-9"},"1701":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-123","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-1","content":"| Field    | Description                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `topics` | Every topic in your account, ordered by `sortOrder` then name. `label` and `description` are the public wording you set on the topic (may be `null`). `subscribed` is `false` when the address opted out. |","table":"table-9"},"1702":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-124","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-response-1","content":"`topics` includes topics you have not published on NorthRelay's hosted preference centre; filter them in your page if needed."},"1703":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-125","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-2","content":"| Code               | Status | When                                  | Fix                         |\n| ------------------ | ------ | ------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400    | The path is not a valid email address | URL-encode the address once |","table":"table-10"},"1704":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-126","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#sdk-2","content":"Both SDKs URL-encode the address for you."},"1705":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-127","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#update-preferences","content":"Apply the choices from your preference page in one call. Returns the updated status in the same shape as Get subscription status."},"1706":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-128","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"Provide at least one of `topics`, `lists` or `unsubscribeAll`. Unknown fields are rejected."},"1707":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-129","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"| Field    | Type   | Description                                                                                                              |\n| -------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `topics` | object | `{ \"<topicId>\": true \\| false }`. `true` removes the opt-out, `false` opts out (and leaves lists tagged with the topic). |","table":"table-11"},"1708":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-130","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"| Field   | Type   | Description                                                                                                        |\n| ------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `lists` | object | `{ \"<listId>\": true \\| false }`. `true` joins the list (the address must already be a contact), `false` leaves it. |","table":"table-11"},"1709":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-131","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"| Field            | Type    | Description                                                                                          |\n| ---------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `unsubscribeAll` | boolean | `true` unsubscribes from everything. When set, `topics` and `lists` in the same request are ignored. |","table":"table-11"},"1710":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-132","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"| Field         | Type    | Description                                                               |\n| ------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `resubscribe` | boolean | Required when joining a list for someone who unsubscribed from everything |","table":"table-11"},"1711":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-133","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"| Field     | Type   | Description                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `consent` | object | `{ ip?, userAgent?, text? }`, recorded when the change re-subscribes the contact. When `resubscribe` is `true` and `consent` is omitted, the request's IP address is recorded. |","table":"table-11"},"1712":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-134","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"Notes:"},"1713":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-135","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"Turning a topic back on does not lift a global unsubscribe. To bring back someone who unsubscribed from everything, join a list with `resubscribe: true`, or call Subscribe with `resubscribe: true`."},"1714":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-136","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#request-body-2","content":"Changes fire `contact.subscribed`, `contact.unsubscribed`, `list.member_added` and `list.member_removed` webhooks with `method: \"api\"` or `source: \"API\"`."},"1715":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-137","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#example-request-3","content":"The response is the full status object shown under Get subscription status."},"1716":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-138","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-3","content":"| Code               | Status | When                                                                         | Fix                       |\n| ------------------ | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400    | Invalid email, unknown field, or none of `topics`, `lists`, `unsubscribeAll` | Send at least one of them |","table":"table-12"},"1717":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-139","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-3","content":"| Code             | Status | When                             | Fix                                            |\n| ---------------- | ------ | -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `LIST_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | A list id is not in your account | Check the id with `GET /api/v1/contacts/lists` |","table":"table-12"},"1718":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-140","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-3","content":"| Code              | Status | When                              | Fix                                                |\n| ----------------- | ------ | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `TOPIC_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | A topic id is not in your account | Check the id with `GET /api/v1/suppression-groups` |","table":"table-12"},"1719":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-141","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-3","content":"| Code                | Status | When                                                | Fix                                                  |\n| ------------------- | ------ | --------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CONTACT_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | Joining a list for an address that is not a contact | Subscribe it first with `POST /api/v1/subscriptions` |","table":"table-12"},"1720":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-142","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-3","content":"| Code                     | Status | When                                                                               | Fix                                           |\n| ------------------------ | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `RECIPIENT_UNSUBSCRIBED` | 409    | Joining a list for someone who unsubscribed from everything, without `resubscribe` | Pass `\"resubscribe\": true` with fresh consent |","table":"table-12"},"1721":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-143","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-3","content":"| Code                   | Status | When                                                                             | Fix                              |\n| ---------------------- | ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `RECIPIENT_SUPPRESSED` | 409    | Joining a list for an address that bounced, complained or is manually suppressed | Cannot be overridden by this API |","table":"table-12"},"1722":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-144","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-3","content":"| Code              | Status | When                                     | Fix                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `CONTACT_BLOCKED` | 409    | The contact is `COMPLAINED` or `CLEANED` | Only re-add with fresh, documented consent |","table":"table-12"},"1723":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-145","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#sdk-3","content":"Python takes `unsubscribe_all=True` for `unsubscribeAll` and raises `ValueError` before calling the API when none of `topics`, `lists` or `unsubscribe_all` is given."},"1724":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-146","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#resend-confirmation","content":"Send the double opt-in email again for a `PENDING` contact that was subscribed through this API, and move the link's expiry to 7 days from now."},"1725":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-147","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#resend-confirmation","content":"No request body."},"1726":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-148","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-4","content":"| Code               | Status | When                                  | Fix                         |\n| ------------------ | ------ | ------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400    | The path is not a valid email address | URL-encode the address once |","table":"table-13"},"1727":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-149","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-4","content":"| Code                | Status | When                         | Fix                                                  |\n| ------------------- | ------ | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CONTACT_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | The address is not a contact | Subscribe it first with `POST /api/v1/subscriptions` |","table":"table-13"},"1728":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-150","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#errors-4","content":"| Code                      | Status | When                                                                                        | Fix                                                                      |\n| ------------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `NO_PENDING_CONFIRMATION` | 409    | The contact is not `PENDING`, is already confirmed, or was subscribed through a signup form | Subscribe it again with `\"doubleOptIn\": true` to send a new confirmation |","table":"table-13"},"1729":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-151","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#sdk-4","content":"Neither SDK retries `subscribe` or `resendConfirmation` automatically, because a retry could send a second confirmation email."},"1730":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-152","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#unsubscribe-links","content":"Marketing mail from NorthRelay carries a signed, per-recipient unsubscribe token:"},"1731":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-153","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#unsubscribe-links","content":"Campaign mail: the `{{unsubscribe_url}}` template variable, plus `List-Unsubscribe` and `List-Unsubscribe-Post` headers (RFC 8058)."},"1732":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-154","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#unsubscribe-links","content":"API mail on a marketing message stream: NorthRelay injects the unsubscribe footer and the same headers automatically."},"1733":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-155","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#unsubscribe-links","content":"The unsubscribe link has the form `https://track.north-pipe.ca/u/{token}`. The token identifies your account and the recipient, so the endpoints below need no API key. Unsubscribes from API mail are attributed to your account and fire `contact.unsubscribed` even when the recipient is not one of your contacts."},"1734":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-156","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#unsubscribe-links","content":"Campaign templates can also use `{{preferences_url}}`, a signed link to NorthRelay's hosted preference centre where the recipient can choose topics or unsubscribe from everything."},"1735":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-157","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"If you host your own unsubscribe landing page, send the token and the recipient's choice here. This endpoint is public; the token is the authentication."},"1736":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-158","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"| Field   | Type   | Required | Description                         |\n| ------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `token` | string | Yes      | The token from the unsubscribe link |","table":"table-14"},"1737":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-159","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"| Field   | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                          |\n| ------- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `scope` | string | No       | `all` (default), `list` or `topic`. `category` is accepted as a legacy alias of `topic`, and upper case is accepted. |","table":"table-14"},"1738":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-160","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"| Field    | Type   | Required               | Description       |\n| -------- | ------ | ---------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `listId` | string | When `scope` is `list` | The list to leave |","table":"table-14"},"1739":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-161","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"| Field     | Type   | Required                | Description                                                 |\n| --------- | ------ | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `topicId` | string | When `scope` is `topic` | The topic to opt out of (legacy name: `suppressionGroupId`) |","table":"table-14"},"1740":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-162","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"| Field    | Type   | Required | Description        |\n| -------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `reason` | string | No       | Max 500 characters |","table":"table-14"},"1741":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-163","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"| Code               | Status | When                                                                         | Fix                                                                                 |\n| ------------------ | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400    | `token` missing, body invalid, or `listId` / `topicId` missing for its scope | Send `{ \"token\": \"...\", \"scope\": \"all\" \\| \"list\" \\| \"topic\" }` with the matching id |","table":"table-15"},"1742":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-164","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"| Code            | Status | When                                                               | Fix                                                 |\n| --------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `INVALID_TOKEN` | 400    | The token is forged, malformed or cannot be matched to a recipient | Use the unsubscribe link from the most recent email |","table":"table-15"},"1743":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-165","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"| Code                                 | Status | When                                  | Fix                                  |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------ | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `LIST_NOT_FOUND` / `TOPIC_NOT_FOUND` | 404    | The id is not in the sender's account | Pass an id from the sender's account |","table":"table-15"},"1744":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-166","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"A bare `contactId` is no longer accepted: it let anyone who learned a contact id opt that person out. For opt-outs from your own server use `POST /subscriptions/unsubscribe` with your API key."},"1745":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-167","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#one-click-unsubscribe-rfc-8058","content":"Mailbox providers (Gmail, Yahoo, Outlook) call the one-click URL from the `List-Unsubscribe` header when the recipient presses their built-in \"Unsubscribe\" button; NorthRelay's tracking service forwards those requests here. It unsubscribes the recipient from all marketing mail (webhook `method: \"one_click\"`) and always answers `200`, as RFC 8058 requires, even when the token cannot be resolved. A missing `token` returns `400`."},"1746":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-168","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#one-click-unsubscribe-rfc-8058","content":"`GET /unsubscribe/one-click?token=` does **not** unsubscribe. Link scanners and security gateways prefetch URLs, so a GET redirects (`303`) to the confirmation page, where the recipient presses a button."},"1747":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-169","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#related","content":"Mailing Lists guide: build signup, double opt-in and a preference page end to end"},"1748":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-170","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#related","content":"Contacts API: contacts, lists, members, CSV import"},"1749":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-171","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#related","content":"Suppressions API: topics (suppression groups) and account-level suppressions"},"1750":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-172","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#related","content":"Webhooks: `contact.*`, `list.*`, `email.opened`, `email.clicked`"},"1751":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions","type":"page","content":"Suppressions API","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","API Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions"},"1752":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions-0","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions","content":"Manage account-level suppressions and topics (suppression groups) that stop mail to bounced, complained or opted-out recipients."},"1753":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions-1","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions#suppressions-api","content":"Suppressions API"},"1754":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions-2","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions#how-suppressions-apply-when-you-send","content":"How suppressions apply when you send"},"1755":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions-3","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions#list-suppressions","content":"List Suppressions"},"1756":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions-4","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/suppressions","type":"heading",