uired | Description          |\n| ------------- | ------ | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `description` | string | No       | Up to 500 characters |","table":"table-2"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-63","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#request-body-1","content":"| Field    | Type    | Required | Description                   |\n| -------- | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `active` | boolean | No       | Enable or disable the webhook |","table":"table-2"},"1969":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-64","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#request-body-1","content":"Returns `{ \"webhook\": { ... }, \"message\": \"Webhook updated successfully\" }`."},"1970":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-65","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#delete-webhook","content":"Remove a webhook endpoint. No further events will be delivered."},"1971":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-66","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#get-webhook","content":"Returns `{ \"webhook\": { ... }, \"stats\": { \"totalDeliveries\", \"successfulDeliveries\", \"successRate\" } }`, with delivery stats for the last 24 hours."},"1972":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-67","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#rotate-secret","content":"The new secret is shown once. For one hour, until `previousSecretValidUntil`, deliveries also carry `X-NorthRelay-Signature-Previous`, signed with the old secret, so you can deploy the new secret without dropping events."},"1973":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-68","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#test-webhook","content":"Sends a test event (body `{ \"eventType\": \"<event type>\" }`, default `email.delivered`) to an active webhook and reports the result:"},"1974":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-69","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#test-webhook","content":"When the endpoint cannot be reached, `success` is `false`, `statusCode` is `0` and `errorMessage` says why."},"1975":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-70","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#sdk","content":"See the TypeScript SDK and Python SDK for details."},"1976":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-71","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"Every webhook is an HTTP `POST` with a JSON body. All events share this envelope:"},"1977":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-72","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field       | Type   | Description                                                           |\n| ----------- | ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `eventType` | string | One of the event types. Also sent in the `X-NorthRelay-Event` header. |","table":"table-3"},"1978":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-73","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field       | Type   | Description                                                                                                         |\n| ----------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `messageId` | string | For `email.*` delivery events, the message id. For contact, list and engagement events, a unique id for this event. |","table":"table-3"},"1979":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-74","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field       | Type   | Description                           |\n| ----------- | ------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `timestamp` | string | ISO 8601 time the event was generated |","table":"table-3"},"1980":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-75","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field       | Type   | Description                                       |\n| ----------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `recipient` | string | Recipient (or contact) address, when there is one |","table":"table-3"},"1981":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-76","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field    | Type   | Description                                |\n| -------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `sender` | string | Sender address (`email.*` delivery events) |","table":"table-3"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-77","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field     | Type   | Description                              |\n| --------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `subject` | string | Subject line (`email.*` delivery events) |","table":"table-3"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-78","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field    | Type   | Description                                           |\n| -------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | string | Delivery status, for example `delivered` or `dropped` |","table":"table-3"},"1984":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-79","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field          | Type   | Description                                        |\n| -------------- | ------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `smtpResponse` | string | Response from the receiving server, when available |","table":"table-3"},"1985":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-80","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field                        | Type   | Description                                                           |\n| ---------------------------- | ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bounceReason`, `bounceType` | string | Bounce details on `email.bounced` and `email.dropped`, when available |","table":"table-3"},"1986":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-81","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"| Field     | Type   | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| --------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `details` | object | Event-specific data. For delivery events this is the raw event from the mail server; for the events below its shape is documented. |","table":"table-3"},"1987":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-82","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#payload-format","content":"Fields that do not apply to an event are omitted. Each request also carries `X-NorthRelay-Delivery` (a unique id per delivery attempt) and `X-NorthRelay-Signature`."},"1988":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-83","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contact-list-and-engagement-events","content":"These events let you keep your own application in sync with subscriptions and engagement. They fire for every path that changes a subscription: hosted signup forms, the Subscriptions API, list member changes, unsubscribe links, RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribes and the hosted preference centre. CSV imports and direct contact edits (`POST` or `PATCH /contacts`) do not fire them."},"1989":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-84","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactsubscribed","content":"Someone subscribed, joined lists through a subscribe call, or opted back into a topic."},"1990":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-85","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactsubscribed","content":"| `details` field      | Description |\n| -------------------- | ----------- |\n| `contactId`, `email` | The contact |","table":"table-4"},"1991":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-86","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                                                    |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `source`        | `FORM`, `API`, `IMPORT`, `PREFERENCE_CENTER`, `PLATFORM_SIGNUP` or `DASHBOARD` |","table":"table-4"},"1992":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-87","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                                   |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `listIds`       | Lists the contact was asked to join (may be omitted or empty) |","table":"table-4"},"1993":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-88","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                                    |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `topicIds`      | Topics the contact opted (back) into (may be omitted or empty) |","table":"table-4"},"1994":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-89","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactsubscribed","content":"| `details` field        | Description                                                               |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `requiresConfirmation` | `true` while a double opt-in is outstanding; wait for `contact.confirmed` |","table":"table-4"},"1995":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-90","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                            |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `status`        | Contact status after the change: `PENDING` or `ACTIVE` |","table":"table-4"},"1996":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-91","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactsubscribed","content":"| `details` field              | Description                                                                                          |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `formId`, `listId`, `fields` | Signup-form submissions only: the form, its list (kept for older consumers) and the submitted fields |","table":"table-4"},"1997":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-92","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactconfirmed","content":"The recipient clicked the double opt-in link."},"1998":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-93","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactconfirmed","content":"`formId` is `null` when the subscription came from the Subscriptions API."},"1999":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-94","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"The recipient unsubscribed from everything, from one list, or from one topic. Fires even when the recipient is not one of your contacts (for example an unsubscribe from API-sent marketing mail)."},"2000":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-95","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                   |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `contactEmail`  | The address that unsubscribed |","table":"table-5"},"2001":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-96","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                              |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contactId`     | The contact, or `null` when the address is not a contact |","table":"table-5"},"2002":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-97","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                         |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `scope`         | `all` (no marketing mail at all), `list` or `topic` |","table":"table-5"},"2003":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-98","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                        |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `listId`        | The list left, for `scope: \"list\"` |","table":"table-5"},"2004":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-99","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                  |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `topicId`       | The topic opted out of, for `scope: \"topic\"` |","table":"table-5"},"2005":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-100","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `method`        | `one_click` (mailbox provider button, or the button on NorthRelay's hosted unsubscribe page), `link` (your own unsubscribe page via `POST /unsubscribe`), `preference_center`, `api`, `dashboard`, `platform_settings` or `complaint` |","table":"table-5"},"2006":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-101","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                        |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `campaignId`    | The campaign the unsubscribe came from, when known |","table":"table-5"},"2007":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-102","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description           |\n| --------------- | --------------------- |\n| `reason`        | Free text, when given |","table":"table-5"},"2008":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-103","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#contactunsubscribed","content":"| `details` field | Description                                            |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `category`      | Legacy alias of `topicId`, kept for existing consumers |","table":"table-5"},"2009":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-104","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#listmember_added-and-listmember_removed","content":"A contact joined or left a list. `list.member_removed` fires both when a recipient unsubscribes from a list (or from a topic the list is tagged with) and when you remove a member."},"2010":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-105","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#listmember_added-and-listmember_removed","content":"`source` is the subscription source (`FORM`, `API`, `IMPORT`, `PREFERENCE_CENTER`, `PLATFORM_SIGNUP`, `DASHBOARD`), or `UNSUBSCRIBE` when the recipient left by unsubscribing. Owner removals through the API use `API`."},"2011":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-106","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#emailopened-and-emailclicked","content":"A person opened a message or clicked a tracked link. Opens and clicks classified as bots (security scanners, link prefetchers, privacy proxies) are not sent. They fire for campaign mail and for API mail with tracking: marketing-stream API mail is tracked by default (opt out with `track: false`), transactional API mail only with `track: true`."},"2012":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-107","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#emailopened-and-emailclicked","content":"| `details` field | Description       |\n| --------------- | ----------------- |\n| `email`         | Recipient address |","table":"table-6"},"2013":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-108","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#emailopened-and-emailclicked","content":"| `details` field           | Description           |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `contactId`, `campaignId` | Set for campaign mail |","table":"table-6"},"2014":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-109","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#emailopened-and-emailclicked","content":"| `details` field | Description                                           |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `trackingId`    | Set for API mail: the tracking id of the sent message |","table":"table-6"},"2015":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-110","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#emailopened-and-emailclicked","content":"| `details` field | Description                             |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `url`           | The clicked link (`email.clicked` only) |","table":"table-6"},"2016":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-111","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#emailopened-and-emailclicked","content":"| `details` field | Description                  |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `userAgent`     | Client user agent, or `null` |","table":"table-6"},"2017":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-112","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#emailopened-and-emailclicked","content":"| `details` field  | Description    |\n| ---------------- | -------------- |\n| `engagementType` | Always `HUMAN` |","table":"table-6"},"2018":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-113","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#emailopened-and-emailclicked","content":"For API mail, `email.opened` fires once per message and recipient; repeat opens are not sent. Clicks fire every time. For campaign mail every human open is sent."},"2019":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-114","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#signature-verification","content":"Every webhook request includes an `X-NorthRelay-Signature` header containing an HMAC-SHA256 signature computed from the raw request body and your webhook secret."},"2020":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-115","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#signature-verification","content":"**Always verify signatures** to ensure requests originate from NorthRelay and have not been tampered with."},"2021":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-116","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#verification-algorithm","content":"Extract the `X-NorthRelay-Signature` header value"},"2022":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-117","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#verification-algorithm","content":"Compute HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body using your webhook `secret` as the key"},"2023":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-118","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#verification-algorithm","content":"Compare the computed signature with the header value using a timing-safe comparison"},"2024":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-119","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#retry-policy","content":"If your endpoint does not respond with a `2xx` status code within 10 seconds, NorthRelay retries the delivery:"},"2025":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-120","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#retry-policy","content":"| Attempt   | Delay      |\n| --------- | ---------- |\n| 1st retry | 30 seconds |","table":"table-7"},"2026":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-121","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#retry-policy","content":"| Attempt   | Delay     |\n| --------- | --------- |\n| 2nd retry | 2 minutes |","table":"table-7"},"2027":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-122","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#retry-policy","content":"| Attempt   | Delay      |\n| --------- | ---------- |\n| 3rd retry | 15 minutes |","table":"table-7"},"2028":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-123","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#retry-policy","content":"| Attempt   | Delay  |\n| --------- | ------ |\n| 4th retry | 1 hour |","table":"table-7"},"2029":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-124","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#retry-policy","content":"| Attempt   | Delay   |\n| --------- | ------- |\n| 5th retry | 4 hours |","table":"table-7"},"2030":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-125","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#retry-policy","content":"After 5 failed retries, the event is marked as failed. Failed events are visible in **Dashboard > Webhooks > Event Log** for 30 days."},"2031":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-126","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#best-practices","content":"**Respond quickly.** Return `200` immediately and process the event asynchronously. Do not perform heavy work in the request handler."},"2032":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-127","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#best-practices","content":"**Handle duplicates.** Deduplicate on `eventType`, `messageId` and `recipient`. The same event may be delivered more than once, and a contact change can arrive before or after a related `list.*` event; read the current state with `GET /subscriptions/{email}` when order matters."},"2033":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-128","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#best-practices","content":"**Verify signatures.** Always validate the `X-NorthRelay-Signature` header."},"2034":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-129","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#best-practices","content":"**Use HTTPS.** Webhook URLs must use HTTPS. HTTP endpoints are rejected."},"2035":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks-130","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/webhooks#best-practices","content":"**Log failures.** Monitor your webhook endpoint health in the dashboard."},"2036":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"page","content":"Billing FAQ","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","Billing"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq"},"2037":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-0","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq","content":"Frequently asked questions about NorthRelay billing, plan changes, and payments"},"2038":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-1","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#billing-faq","content":"Billing FAQ"},"2039":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-2","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#plan-changes","content":"Plan Changes"},"2040":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-3","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#can-i-switch-plans-at-any-time","content":"Can I switch plans at any time?"},"2041":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-4","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#is-my-billing-prorated-when-i-upgrade","content":"Is my billing prorated when I upgrade?"},"2042":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-5","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#is-my-billing-prorated-when-i-downgrade","content":"Is my billing prorated when I downgrade?"},"2043":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-6","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-custom-domains-if-i-downgrade","content":"What happens to my custom domains if I downgrade?"},"2044":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-7","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-webhooks-if-i-downgrade","content":"What happens to my webhooks if I downgrade?"},"2045":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-8","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-team-members-if-i-downgrade-below-pro","content":"What happens to my team members if I downgrade below Pro?"},"2046":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-9","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#quotas--limits","content":"Quotas & Limits"},"2047":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-10","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-if-i-exceed-my-monthly-email-quota","content":"What happens if I exceed my monthly email quota?"},"2048":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-11","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#do-unused-emails-roll-over-to-the-next-month","content":"Do unused emails roll over to the next month?"},"2049":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-12","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#is-there-an-overage-option-instead-of-upgrading","content":"Is there an overage option instead of upgrading?"},"2050":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-13","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#payments","content":"Payments"},"2051":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-14","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-payment-methods-do-you-accept","content":"What payment methods do you accept?"},"2052":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-15","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-currency-are-charges-in","content":"What currency are charges in?"},"2053":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-16","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#when-am-i-charged","content":"When am I charged?"},"2054":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-17","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-if-my-payment-fails","content":"What if my payment fails?"},"2055":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-18","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#can-i-pay-annually","content":"Can I pay annually?"},"2056":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-19","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#refunds","content":"Refunds"},"2057":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-20","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-is-your-refund-policy","content":"What is your refund policy?"},"2058":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-21","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#how-do-i-request-a-refund","content":"How do I request a refund?"},"2059":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-22","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#free-tier","content":"Free Tier"},"2060":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-23","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-are-the-free-tier-limitations","content":"What are the Free tier limitations?"},"2061":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-24","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#do-i-need-a-credit-card-for-the-free-tier","content":"Do I need a credit card for the free tier?"},"2062":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-25","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#enterprise","content":"Enterprise"},"2063":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-26","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#how-does-enterprise-pricing-work","content":"How does Enterprise pricing work?"},"2064":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-27","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#can-i-get-a-dedicated-ip","content":"Can I get a dedicated IP?"},"2065":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-28","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#do-you-offer-non-profit-or-startup-discounts","content":"Do you offer non-profit or startup discounts?"},"2066":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-29","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/billing/faq#related","content":"Related"},"2067":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-30","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#can-i-switch-plans-at-any-time","content":"Yes. You can upgrade or downgrade your plan at any time from **Dashboard > Billing > Change Plan**."},"2068":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-31","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#can-i-switch-plans-at-any-time","content":"**Upgrades** take effect immediately. You get instant access to the new tier's features and sending limits."},"2069":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-32","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#can-i-switch-plans-at-any-time","content":"**Downgrades** take effect at the end of your current billing cycle. You keep your current features until then."},"2070":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-33","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#is-my-billing-prorated-when-i-upgrade","content":"Yes. When you upgrade mid-cycle, you are charged the prorated difference for the remaining days in your billing period. For example, if you upgrade from Micro ($12/mo) to Pro ($29/mo) halfway through your cycle, you pay approximately $8.50 for the remaining half-month."},"2071":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-34","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#is-my-billing-prorated-when-i-downgrade","content":"No. Downgrades take effect at the end of your current billing cycle. You are not refunded for the remaining days on your current plan, but you retain full access to your current tier's features until the cycle ends."},"2072":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-35","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-custom-domains-if-i-downgrade","content":"Custom domains are a Starter+ feature, and each tier allows a different number (1 / 2 / 5 / 20). If you downgrade to Free, or to a tier with fewer domains than you have:"},"2073":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-36","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-custom-domains-if-i-downgrade","content":"Domains above the new limit are **deactivated** (not deleted) at the end of the billing cycle"},"2074":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-37","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-custom-domains-if-i-downgrade","content":"Emails from a deactivated domain are rejected with `FORBIDDEN_SENDER`; use a remaining verified domain or your NorthRelay system subdomain instead"},"2075":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-38","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-custom-domains-if-i-downgrade","content":"Your domain configuration is preserved -- if you upgrade again, your domains reactivate without needing to re-verify DNS"},"2076":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-39","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-webhooks-if-i-downgrade","content":"Webhooks are a Starter+ feature with a per-tier count (1 / 3 / 10 / unlimited). If you downgrade below your current count:"},"2077":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-40","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-webhooks-if-i-downgrade","content":"Webhook endpoints above the new limit are **paused** at the end of the billing cycle"},"2078":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-41","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-webhooks-if-i-downgrade","content":"No events are delivered while paused"},"2079":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-42","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-webhooks-if-i-downgrade","content":"Webhook configurations are preserved -- upgrading reactivates them"},"2080":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-43","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-team-members-if-i-downgrade-below-pro","content":"Team members are a Pro+ feature. If you downgrade:"},"2081":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-44","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-team-members-if-i-downgrade-below-pro","content":"Team member access is **revoked** at the end of the billing cycle"},"2082":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-45","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-to-my-team-members-if-i-downgrade-below-pro","content":"Team member accounts are preserved -- upgrading restores their access"},"2083":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-46","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-if-i-exceed-my-monthly-email-quota","content":"When you reach your monthly sending limit:"},"2084":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-47","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-if-i-exceed-my-monthly-email-quota","content":"Additional send requests return an error: `451 4.7.1 Rate limit exceeded`"},"2085":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-48","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-if-i-exceed-my-monthly-email-quota","content":"The API returns a `QuotaExceededError` with a clear message"},"2086":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-49","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-if-i-exceed-my-monthly-email-quota","content":"Already-queued and in-progress emails continue to deliver"},"2087":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-50","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-if-i-exceed-my-monthly-email-quota","content":"Your dashboard shows a warning when you reach 80% of your quota"},"2088":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-51","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-if-i-exceed-my-monthly-email-quota","content":"Your quota resets at the start of your next billing cycle"},"2089":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-52","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-happens-if-i-exceed-my-monthly-email-quota","content":"You can upgrade your plan at any time to get a higher quota immediately."},"2090":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-53","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#do-unused-emails-roll-over-to-the-next-month","content":"No. Email quotas reset at the start of each billing cycle. Unused emails do not carry over."},"2091":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-54","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#is-there-an-overage-option-instead-of-upgrading","content":"Not currently. If you regularly exceed your quota, upgrading to the next tier is the recommended approach. Enterprise plans can include custom quota arrangements -- contact sales."},"2092":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-55","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-payment-methods-do-you-accept","content":"NorthRelay accepts Visa, Mastercard, and American Express credit and debit cards. All payments are processed securely through Stripe."},"2093":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-56","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-currency-are-charges-in","content":"All charges are in **CAD** (Canadian dollars). Prices are tax-exclusive; GST/HST and, for Québec, QST are added at checkout."},"2094":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-57","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#when-am-i-charged","content":"You are charged on the same day each month, based on the date you first subscribed. For example, if you signed up on March 15, you are charged on the 15th of each month."},"2095":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-58","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-if-my-payment-fails","content":"If a payment fails:"},"2096":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-59","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-if-my-payment-fails","content":"You receive an email notification"},"2097":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-60","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-if-my-payment-fails","content":"Stripe automatically retries after 3 days, then again after 5 days"},"2098":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-61","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-if-my-payment-fails","content":"If all retries fail, your account is downgraded to the Free tier"},"2099":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-62","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-if-my-payment-fails","content":"You can resolve it at any time by updating your payment method and retrying"},"2100":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-63","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-if-my-payment-fails","content":"No data is lost during a payment failure. Your account, domains, templates, and contacts are all preserved."},"2101":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-64","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#can-i-pay-annually","content":"Annual billing is not currently available for self-service plans. Enterprise customers can arrange annual billing -- contact sales."},"2102":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-65","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-is-your-refund-policy","content":"NorthRelay offers a **14-day money-back guarantee** on your first payment for any paid plan. If you are not satisfied within 14 days of your first charge, contact support for a full refund."},"2103":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-66","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-is-your-refund-policy","content":"After the 14-day window:"},"2104":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-67","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-is-your-refund-policy","content":"Monthly charges are **not refundable** once the billing cycle has started"},"2105":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-68","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-is-your-refund-policy","content":"Downgrades take effect at the end of the cycle (no partial refund)"},"2106":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-69","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-is-your-refund-policy","content":"If there is a service issue on NorthRelay's end (outage, billing error), refunds or credits are handled on a case-by-case basis"},"2107":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-70","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#how-do-i-request-a-refund","content":"Email support@northrelay.ca with your account email and the reason for your request. Refund requests within the 14-day window are processed within 5-10 business days."},"2108":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-71","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-are-the-free-tier-limitations","content":"The Free tier includes:"},"2109":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-72","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-are-the-free-tier-limitations","content":"3,000 emails per month"},"2110":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-73","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-are-the-free-tier-limitations","content":"Sends from a NorthRelay system subdomain only (no custom domains)"},"2111":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-74","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-are-the-free-tier-limitations","content":"No inbox access"},"2112":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-75","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-are-the-free-tier-limitations","content":"Full API and SDK access"},"2113":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-76","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-are-the-free-tier-limitations","content":"No webhooks, campaigns or team features"},"2114":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-77","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#what-are-the-free-tier-limitations","content":"There is no time limit on the Free tier. You can use it indefinitely."},"2115":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-78","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#do-i-need-a-credit-card-for-the-free-tier","content":"No. The Free tier requires no credit card and no payment information."},"2116":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-79","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#how-does-enterprise-pricing-work","content":"Enterprise pricing is custom based on your requirements:"},"2117":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-80","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#how-does-enterprise-pricing-work","content":"**Volume:** Sending limits above the Scale tier"},"2118":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-81","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#how-does-enterprise-pricing-work","content":"**Support:** Priority support with guaranteed response times, dedicated account manager"},"2119":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-82","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#how-does-enterprise-pricing-work","content":"**Compliance:** Custom SLA, data processing agreements, security reviews"},"2120":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-83","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#how-does-enterprise-pricing-work","content":"Contact sales for a quote."},"2121":{"id":"/docs/billing/faq-84","page_id":"/docs/billing/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/billing/faq#can-i-get-a-dedicated-ip","content":"No. NorthRelay sends all mail from one protected IP and does not offer dedicated IPs on any plan. For typical volumes a warm, continuously monitored IP with a strict sender policy (verified domains only, one-click unsubscribe, automatic b