tation-monitoring-18","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-spam-complaint-rate-is-high","content":"If Your Spam Complaint Rate Is High"},"2534":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-19","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-delivery-failure-rate-is-high","content":"If Your Delivery Failure Rate Is High"},"2535":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-20","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-score-dropped-suddenly","content":"If Your Score Dropped Suddenly"},"2536":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-21","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"2537":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-22","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#related","content":"Related"},"2538":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-23","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#reputation-monitoring","content":"NorthRelay continuously monitors your sender reputation and automatically detects delivery issues. Your reputation score directly affects whether your emails land in the inbox or get filtered to spam."},"2539":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-24","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#understanding-sender-reputation","content":"Every email you send contributes to your sender reputation -- a score that mailbox providers (Gmail, Outlook, Yahoo, etc.) use to decide whether to accept, filter, or reject your messages. NorthRelay tracks this internally and provides a real-time view in your dashboard."},"2540":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-25","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#understanding-sender-reputation","content":"A high reputation means:"},"2541":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-26","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#understanding-sender-reputation","content":"Better inbox placement rates"},"2542":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-27","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#understanding-sender-reputation","content":"Fewer emails landing in spam"},"2543":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-28","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#understanding-sender-reputation","content":"Higher delivery speeds (less throttling by receivers)"},"2544":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-29","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#understanding-sender-reputation","content":"Protection of the shared sending IP everyone relies on"},"2545":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-30","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#reputation-score","content":"Your reputation score starts at **100** and adjusts based on your sending behavior. The score is recalculated hourly via automated snapshots."},"2546":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-31","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-ranges","content":"| Range      | Status    | Meaning                                                 |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **90-100** | Excellent | Top-tier deliverability. Keep doing what you are doing. |","table":"table-0"},"2547":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-32","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-ranges","content":"| Range     | Status | Meaning                                       |\n| --------- | ------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| **70-89** | Good   | Healthy sending. Minor improvements possible. |","table":"table-0"},"2548":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-33","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-ranges","content":"| Range     | Status | Meaning                                                |\n| --------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **50-69** | Fair   | Deliverability may be impacted. Review your practices. |","table":"table-0"},"2549":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-34","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-ranges","content":"| Range     | Status | Meaning                                               |\n| --------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| **30-49** | Poor   | Significant delivery issues. Immediate action needed. |","table":"table-0"},"2550":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-35","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-ranges","content":"| Range    | Status   | Meaning                                                              |\n| -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **0-29** | Critical | Most emails will be rejected or filtered. Sending may be restricted. |","table":"table-0"},"2551":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-36","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-calculation","content":"The score is computed from a base of 100 with deductions based on negative signals:"},"2552":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-37","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-calculation","content":"| Factor          | Weight | Description                                                |\n| --------------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Bounce Rate** | High   | Percentage of emails that hard-bounced (invalid addresses) |","table":"table-1"},"2553":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-38","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-calculation","content":"| Factor              | Weight | Description                                            |\n| ------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Spam Complaints** | High   | Percentage of recipients who marked your email as spam |","table":"table-1"},"2554":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-39","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-calculation","content":"| Factor                | Weight | Description                                                        |\n| --------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Delivery Failures** | Medium | Percentage of emails that failed to deliver (timeouts, rejections) |","table":"table-1"},"2555":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-40","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-calculation","content":"| Factor         | Weight | Description                                          |\n| -------------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Engagement** | Low    | Open and click rates relative to your sending volume |","table":"table-1"},"2556":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-41","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-calculation","content":"Deductions are proportional. For example, a 5% bounce rate has a larger impact than a 1% bounce rate. The formula weights recent activity more heavily than historical data to reflect your current sending health."},"2557":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-42","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#dashboard-overview","content":"Navigate to **Dashboard > Reputation** to see:"},"2558":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-43","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#current-score","content":"A large gauge displays your current score with color coding (green, yellow, orange, red) and the trend direction (improving, stable, declining) compared to 24 hours ago."},"2559":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-44","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#score-history","content":"A line chart shows your daily reputation score over the past 30 days. Use this to spot trends and correlate score changes with sending activity or incident events."},"2560":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-45","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#active-incidents","content":"A list of any currently open incidents that are affecting your reputation, with severity indicators and recommended actions."},"2561":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-46","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#key-metrics","content":"Four metric cards show your current:"},"2562":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-47","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#key-metrics","content":"**Bounce Rate** -- with threshold indicator"},"2563":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-48","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#key-metrics","content":"**Spam Complaint Rate** -- with threshold indicator"},"2564":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-49","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#key-metrics","content":"**Delivery Success Rate** -- percentage of emails accepted by receivers"},"2565":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-50","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#key-metrics","content":"**Engagement Rate** -- opens and clicks as a percentage of delivered emails"},"2566":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-51","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#incident-detection","content":"NorthRelay automatically detects problems and creates incidents when metrics cross defined thresholds."},"2567":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-52","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#incident-types","content":"| Type               | Trigger                       | Description                                                  |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `HIGH_BOUNCE_RATE` | Bounce rate exceeds threshold | Too many emails are bouncing, indicating list quality issues |","table":"table-2"},"2568":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-53","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#incident-types","content":"| Type              | Trigger                          | Description                                |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `SPAM_COMPLAINTS` | Complaint rate exceeds threshold | Recipients are marking your emails as spam |","table":"table-2"},"2569":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-54","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#incident-types","content":"| Type                | Trigger                                 | Description                                                        |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `HIGH_FAILURE_RATE` | Delivery failure rate exceeds threshold | Emails are failing to deliver due to server rejections or timeouts |","table":"table-2"},"2570":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-55","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#incident-types","content":"| Type         | Trigger                                     | Description                                                                    |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `SCORE_DROP` | Score drops significantly in a short period | Sudden reputation decline detected, even if no single metric is over threshold |","table":"table-2"},"2571":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-56","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#severity-levels","content":"| Severity    | Meaning                                    | Action                                          |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| **WARNING** | A metric has crossed its warning threshold | Review your sending practices and contact lists |","table":"table-3"},"2572":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-57","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#severity-levels","content":"| Severity     | Meaning                             | Action                                                   |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **CRITICAL** | A metric has reached a severe level | Immediate action required to prevent delivery disruption |","table":"table-3"},"2573":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-58","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#thresholds","content":"| Metric      | Warning | Critical |\n| ----------- | ------- | -------- |\n| Bounce Rate | > 3%    | > 8%     |","table":"table-4"},"2574":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-59","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#thresholds","content":"| Metric              | Warning | Critical |\n| ------------------- | ------- | -------- |\n| Spam Complaint Rate | > 0.1%  | > 0.3%   |","table":"table-4"},"2575":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-60","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#thresholds","content":"| Metric                | Warning | Critical |\n| --------------------- | ------- | -------- |\n| Delivery Failure Rate | > 5%    | > 15%    |","table":"table-4"},"2576":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-61","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#thresholds","content":"| Metric           | Warning     | Critical    |\n| ---------------- | ----------- | ----------- |\n| Score Drop (24h) | > 15 points | > 30 points |","table":"table-4"},"2577":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-62","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#auto-resolution","content":"Incidents automatically resolve when the triggering metric returns below its warning threshold. You do not need to manually close incidents. The resolution is noted in the incident history with a timestamp."},"2578":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-63","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-bounce-rate-is-high","content":"**Clean your contact list.** Remove addresses that have hard-bounced. NorthRelay automatically adds hard bounces to your suppression list."},"2579":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-64","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-bounce-rate-is-high","content":"**Use double opt-in.** Require email confirmation before adding contacts to your list."},"2580":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-65","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-bounce-rate-is-high","content":"**Validate emails at collection.** Use email syntax validation on signup forms."},"2581":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-66","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-bounce-rate-is-high","content":"**Remove inactive subscribers.** Contacts who have not engaged in 6+ months are more likely to become invalid."},"2582":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-67","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-spam-complaint-rate-is-high","content":"**Only send to opted-in recipients.** Never purchase email lists."},"2583":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-68","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-spam-complaint-rate-is-high","content":"**Include a visible unsubscribe link.** Make it easy to opt out -- this reduces complaints."},"2584":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-69","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-spam-complaint-rate-is-high","content":"**Set expectations at signup.** Tell subscribers what content they will receive and how often."},"2585":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-70","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-spam-complaint-rate-is-high","content":"**Honor unsubscribes immediately.** Process opt-outs within the same sending cycle."},"2586":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-71","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-spam-complaint-rate-is-high","content":"**Segment your audience.** Send relevant content to each group rather than blasting everyone."},"2587":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-72","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-delivery-failure-rate-is-high","content":"**Check your DNS configuration.** Use the Pre-Flight Check to validate SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records."},"2588":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-73","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-delivery-failure-rate-is-high","content":"**Verify your sending domain.** Unverified domains have lower trust with receivers."},"2589":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-74","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-delivery-failure-rate-is-high","content":"**Check the Blocklist Monitor.** Your IP or domain may be listed on a blocklist."},"2590":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-75","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-delivery-failure-rate-is-high","content":"**Reduce sending volume temporarily.** If you are being throttled, slow down and gradually ramp back up."},"2591":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-76","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-score-dropped-suddenly","content":"**Check for new incidents.** The incidents panel will tell you which metric triggered the drop."},"2592":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-77","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-score-dropped-suddenly","content":"**Review recent sending activity.** Did you send to a new or untested list?"},"2593":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-78","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#if-your-score-dropped-suddenly","content":"**Check for infrastructure issues.** Use the Connectivity Doctor to verify SMTP connectivity."},"2594":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-79","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#best-practices","content":"**Warm up new domains gradually.** Start with small volumes (100-500/day) and increase over 2-4 weeks."},"2595":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-80","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#best-practices","content":"**Monitor your dashboard weekly.** Catch trends before they become incidents."},"2596":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-81","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#best-practices","content":"**Keep bounce rate under 2%.** This is the industry standard for healthy sending."},"2597":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-82","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#best-practices","content":"**Keep complaint rate under 0.08%.** Gmail's threshold for filtering is 0.1%."},"2598":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-83","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#best-practices","content":"**Segment by engagement.** Send more frequently to engaged contacts, less to inactive ones."},"2599":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-84","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#best-practices","content":"**Authenticate everything.** SPF, DKIM, and DMARC should all pass for every email."},"2600":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-85","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#related","content":"Diagnostic Tools for troubleshooting delivery issues"},"2601":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-86","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#related","content":"Domain Verification for setting up proper authentication"},"2602":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-87","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#related","content":"Sending Infrastructure for how NorthRelay protects its sending IP"},"2603":{"id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring-88","page_id":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/reputation-monitoring#related","content":"Plans & Pricing for tier-specific reputation features"},"2604":{"id":"/docs/features/studio","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"page","content":"NorthRelay Studio","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio"},"2605":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-0","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio","content":"One place for email templates and brands — visual or HTML editing, versioned releases, brand previews, and the same templates from the dashboard, the API, SDKs, MCP and embedded apps"},"2606":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-1","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#northrelay-studio","content":"NorthRelay Studio"},"2607":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-2","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"What you get"},"2608":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-3","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#account-templates-and-application-templates","content":"Account templates and application templates"},"2609":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-4","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#sending-with-a-template","content":"Sending with a template"},"2610":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-5","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#from-code","content":"From code"},"2611":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-6","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"API surface"},"2612":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-7","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#installing-templates-into-another-account","content":"Installing templates into another account"},"2613":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-8","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#embedding-studio-in-your-product","content":"Embedding Studio in your product"},"2614":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-9","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#legacy-apis","content":"Legacy APIs"},"2615":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-10","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/studio#plans","content":"Plans"},"2616":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-11","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#northrelay-studio","content":"NorthRelay Studio is where your email **templates** and **brands** live. Every template, whether you build it in the dashboard, adopt it from the gallery or create it from code, is a versioned design: you edit a draft, review it, and publish an immutable release that sends use. Studio is included from the **Micro plan** ($12/mo)."},"2617":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-12","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#northrelay-studio","content":"Open it from the sidebar: **Studio** → Overview, Templates, Brands, Assets, Applications and Activity."},"2618":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-13","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability    | What it means for you                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Templates** | Build visually with blocks or write HTML with Handlebars variables. Start blank or from the gallery (authentication, notifications, billing, marketing). |","table":"table-0"},"2619":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-14","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability | What it means for you                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Brands** | Colours, logo, fonts, sender, compliance contact, footer, social links, custom variables and the unsubscribe page. Every template reads them as `{{theme.*}}`. Contrast checks warn when text would be hard to read. |","table":"table-0"},"2620":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-15","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability  | What it means for you                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Preview** | Rendered by the same engine that sends: desktop, mobile, simulated dark mode and plain text, with sample data from the variable schema or your own values. Preview any template with another brand before you switch. |","table":"table-0"},"2621":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-16","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability           | What it means for you                                                                                          |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Review & publish** | A field-by-field diff against the live release before you publish. Drafts autosave and never affect live mail. |","table":"table-0"},"2622":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-17","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability   | What it means for you                                                            |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Releases** | Each publish is an immutable snapshot. Restore any earlier release in one click. |","table":"table-0"},"2623":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-18","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability | What it means for you                                                                                            |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Usage**  | See which campaigns use a template and how many messages it sent, and which templates and campaigns use a brand. |","table":"table-0"},"2624":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-19","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability     | What it means for you                                                            |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Deliveries** | Every send through a template, from the API or Studio, with its delivery events. |","table":"table-0"},"2625":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-20","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability     | What it means for you                                                                |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Test sends** | Send yourself a test from a verified sender, safely retried with an idempotency key. |","table":"table-0"},"2626":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-21","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability | What it means for you                                                                                                       |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Assets** | Upload a logo (PNG, JPEG or WebP up to 700 KiB). NorthRelay resizes it for email and serves it from an immutable HTTPS URL. |","table":"table-0"},"2627":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-22","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#what-you-get","content":"| Capability       | What it means for you                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Applications** | Products that send through NorthRelay (for example Alteriom Command Center) keep their own templates and brands under an application key, reached with a scoped `nr_app_` credential. |","table":"table-0"},"2628":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-23","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#account-templates-and-application-templates","content":"Your own templates, the ones you create in the dashboard, belong to the reserved application **`account`**. Products can own templates under their own application key. The two differ in how they treat brands and variables:"},"2629":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-24","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#account-templates-and-application-templates","content":"|       | Account templates (`account`)                                            | Application templates (e.g. `command-center`)                                                                                                      |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Brand | Uses the bound brand **live**: edit the brand and the next send uses it. | The brand is **frozen in each release**. After a brand change, the brand editor lists the templates to publish again and can publish them for you. |","table":"table-1"},"2630":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-25","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#account-templates-and-application-templates","content":"|           | Account templates (`account`)                                           | Application templates (e.g. `command-center`)                              |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Variables | Lenient: a missing variable renders empty, extra variables are ignored. | Strict: required variables must be present, unknown variables are refused. |","table":"table-1"},"2631":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-26","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#account-templates-and-application-templates","content":"|        | Account templates (`account`)                                                                             | Application templates (e.g. `command-center`)    |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Sender | Optional on the template; the brand sender is the default, and a send can choose another verified sender. | Must be one of the credential's allowed senders. |","table":"table-1"},"2632":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-27","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#sending-with-a-template","content":"Use the template id with the email API. Nothing changes if you already send this way:"},"2633":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-28","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#sending-with-a-template","content":"The send uses the template's **live release**. A retired template is refused with `TEMPLATE_RETIRED`, a template that was never published with `TEMPLATE_NOT_PUBLISHED`, and missing required variables with `MISSING_TEMPLATE_VARIABLES`; each error names the fix."},"2634":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-29","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#sending-with-a-template","content":"Campaigns pick a template in the campaign wizard and render it with the contact's details, the brand and the unsubscribe links."},"2635":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-30","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#from-code","content":"Everything in Studio is available through `/api/v1/designs`, the SDKs and the MCP server."},"2636":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-31","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#from-code","content":"Every response is `{ success: true, data }` or `{ success: false, error: { code, message } }`. Writes carry `expectedRevision` (designs) or `expectedUpdatedAt` (brands), so two editors get a `409 REVISION_CONFLICT` instead of overwriting each other."},"2637":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-32","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                   | Purpose                                                         |\n| ------ | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| GET    | `/api/v1/capabilities` | Permissions, application and sender restrictions, plan capacity |","table":"table-2"},"2638":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-33","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method    | Path              | Purpose                                           |\n| --------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| GET, POST | `/api/v1/designs` | List templates (filters, cursor) / create a draft |","table":"table-2"},"2639":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-34","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method             | Path                   | Purpose                                                                           |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| GET, PATCH, DELETE | `/api/v1/designs/{id}` | Read / replace the draft (`expectedRevision`) / delete a template that never sent |","table":"table-2"},"2640":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-35","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                           | Purpose                                                                           |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| POST   | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/preview` | Render the draft, the live release or a version; `brandId` previews another brand |","table":"table-2"},"2641":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-36","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                           | Purpose                    |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ | -------------------------- |\n| POST   | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/publish` | Publish `expectedRevision` |","table":"table-2"},"2642":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-37","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                            | Purpose                                    |\n| ------ | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| POST   | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/rollback` | Copy an earlier version into a new release |","table":"table-2"},"2643":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-38","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                            | Purpose                                          |\n| ------ | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| GET    | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/releases` | Release history; `?version=` for a full snapshot |","table":"table-2"},"2644":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-39","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                        | Purpose                                            |\n| ------ | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| POST   | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/send` | Send the live release (`Idempotency-Key` required) |","table":"table-2"},"2645":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-40","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                              | Purpose                                      |\n| ------ | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| GET    | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/deliveries` | Sends through this template and their events |","table":"table-2"},"2646":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-41","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                         | Purpose                                   |\n| ------ | ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| GET    | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/usage` | Campaigns using the template, send counts |","table":"table-2"},"2647":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-42","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                             | Purpose                                         |\n| ------ | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| PATCH  | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/lifecycle` | Retire or restore, with an optional replacement |","table":"table-2"},"2648":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-43","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                         | Purpose      |\n| ------ | ---------------------------- | ------------ |\n| POST   | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/brand` | Bind a brand |","table":"table-2"},"2649":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-44","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                        | Purpose                                               |\n| ------ | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| POST   | `/api/v1/designs/{id}/sync` | Compare with or apply updates from the gallery source |","table":"table-2"},"2650":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-45","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method    | Path                      | Purpose                                               |\n| --------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| GET, POST | `/api/v1/designs/catalog` | Browse the gallery and shared templates / inspect one |","table":"table-2"},"2651":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-46","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                            | Purpose                                            |\n| ------ | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| POST   | `/api/v1/designs/catalog/adopt` | Adopt a starter (`asBlocks` for the visual editor) |","table":"table-2"},"2652":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-47","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method    | Path                     | Purpose              |\n| --------- | ------------------------ | -------------------- |\n| GET, POST | `/api/v1/designs/brands` | List / create brands |","table":"table-2"},"2653":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-48","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method             | Path                          | Purpose                                                      |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| GET, PATCH, DELETE | `/api/v1/designs/brands/{id}` | Read / update (`expectedUpdatedAt`) / delete an unused brand |","table":"table-2"},"2654":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-49","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                                | Purpose                                 |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| GET    | `/api/v1/designs/brands/{id}/usage` | Templates and campaigns using the brand |","table":"table-2"},"2655":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-50","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method | Path                                  | Purpose                           |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| POST   | `/api/v1/designs/brands/{id}/default` | Make an account brand the default |","table":"table-2"},"2656":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-51","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method           | Path                                          | Purpose                                                   |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| GET, PUT, DELETE | `/api/v1/designs/brands/{id}/tracking-domain` | Custom tracking domain (`POST …/verify` checks the CNAME) |","table":"table-2"},"2657":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-52","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method            | Path                     | Purpose                       |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| GET, POST, DELETE | `/api/v1/designs/assets` | List / upload / delete images |","table":"table-2"},"2658":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-53","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"| Method    | Path                       | Purpose                                                                                                                                           |\n| --------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| GET, POST | `/api/v1/designs/manifest` | Export (with a `version` that changes when any draft changes), plan or atomically apply drafts; `publish: true` then publishes each changed entry |","table":"table-2"},"2659":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-54","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"New releases render with `handlebars-email-v2`: values are escaped, template sources are checked on save and publish (no script, iframe, form, event handlers or `javascript:` links), and MJML styles and Outlook conditional comments are kept."},"2660":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-55","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#api-surface","content":"The TypeScript and Python SDKs expose these as `client.designs`, and the MCP server as the `*_email_design*`, `*_email_brand*` and `*_email_asset*` tools."},"2661":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-56","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#installing-templates-into-another-account","content":"A product that sends through its users' own NorthRelay accounts can ship its templates as a manifest: export the application's manifest from the product's account, then apply it with the user's credential into their account (`dryRun: true` to show the plan, then `dryRun: false, publish: true` to install and publish in one call). The export's `version` tells you when an installed copy is behind."},"2662":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-57","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#embedding-studio-in-your-product","content":"`@northrelay/studio-react` renders the same Studio screens (template library, workspace, brands) inside another React app. Your server proxies the Studio API with an application credential, so no NorthRelay key reaches the browser. Alteriom Command Center uses it."},"2663":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-58","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#legacy-apis","content":"`/api/v1/templates` and `/api/v1/brand-theme` keep working until **30 April 2027** and return `Deprecation`, `Sunset` and `Link: rel=\"successor-version\"` headers. Every existing template is now a Studio template with the same id, so `templateId` values in your code stay valid. Move template and brand management to `/api/v1/designs`."},"2664":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-59","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#plans","content":"|               | Free | Starter | Micro | Pro | Scale |\n| ------------- | ---- | ------- | ----- | --- | ----- |\n| Studio access | –    | –       | Yes   | Yes | Yes   |","table":"table-3"},"2665":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-60","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#plans","content":"|           | Free | Starter | Micro | Pro | Scale |\n| --------- | ---- | ------- | ----- | --- | ----- |\n| Templates | –    | –       | 25    | 100 | 500   |","table":"table-3"},"2666":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-61","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#plans","content":"|        | Free | Starter | Micro | Pro | Scale |\n| ------ | ---- | ------- | ----- | --- | ----- |\n| Brands | –    | –       | 3     | 10  | 25    |","table":"table-3"},"2667":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-62","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#plans","content":"|                         | Free | Starter | Micro | Pro | Scale |\n| ----------------------- | ---- | ------- | ----- | --- | ----- |\n| Application credentials | –    | –       | Yes   | Yes | Yes   |","table":"table-3"},"2668":{"id":"/docs/features/studio-63","page_id":"/docs/features/studio","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/studio#plans","content":"See Plans & Pricing for the full ladder."},"2669":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","type":"page","content":"Sending Infrastructure","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system"},"2670":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-0","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","content":"How NorthRelay delivers your mail from one protected IP"},"2671":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-1","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#sending-infrastructure","content":"Sending Infrastructure"},"2672":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-2","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#one-relay-for-everyone","content":"One relay for everyone"},"2673":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-3","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#how-we-protect-its-reputation","content":"How we protect its reputation"},"2674":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-4","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#what-changes-between-tiers","content":"What changes between tiers"},"2675":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-5","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#upgrading","content":"Upgrading"},"2676":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-6","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#previously-the-two-pool-system","content":"Previously: the Two-Pool system"},"2677":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-7","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#sending-infrastructure","content":"> One clean relay, actively protected, shared by every tier."},"2678":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-8","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#one-relay-for-everyone","content":"Every message you send through NorthRelay — on any plan, from any sender domain — leaves through a single sending relay:"},"2679":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-9","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#one-relay-for-everyone","content":"|              |                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------- |\n| **Hostname** | `sovereign.north-pipe.ca` |","table":"table-0"},"2680":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-10","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#one-relay-for-everyone","content":"|          |                |\n| -------- | -------------- |\n| **IPv4** | `76.13.27.101` |","table":"table-0"},"2681":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-11","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#one-relay-for-everyone","content":"|          |                           |\n| -------- | ------------------------- |\n| **HELO** | `sovereign.north-pipe.ca` |","table":"table-0"},"2682":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-12","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#one-relay-for-everyone","content":"|                 |                              |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| **SPF include** | `include:_spf.north-pipe.ca` |","table":"table-0"},"2683":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-13","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#one-relay-for-everyone","content":"You connect to `smtp.north-pipe.ca` (or the REST API); NorthRelay queues your message and hands it to the relay, which signs it with DKIM and delivers it to the recipient's mail server. There is nothing to choose and nothing to configure — the path is the same for every account."},"2684":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-14","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#how-we-protect-its-reputation","content":"A single IP only works if it stays clean. These protections are enforced in code on every message:"},"2685":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-15","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#how-we-protect-its-reputation","content":"**Verified-From policy** — you can only send from a domain you have added and verified in your dashboard (or a subdomain of one). Requests from any other address are rejected with `403 FORBIDDEN_SENDER` and a message telling you which domain to verify. Nobody can spoof a domain they don't own."},"2686":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-16","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#how-we-protect-its-reputation","content":"**One-click unsubscribe** — every marketing and campaign message carries RFC 8058 `List-Unsubscribe` headers, so recipients can opt out with one click instead of reporting spam."},"2687":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-17","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#how-we-protect-its-reputation","content":"**Bounce and complaint suppression** — hard bounces and spam complaints are added to your suppression list automatically and never mailed again."},"2688":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-18","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#how-we-protect-its-reputation","content":"**Hourly delivery canary** — every hour NorthRelay sends a real message through the full sending path to a monitored mailbox and checks that it arrives with SPF, DKIM and DMARC passing. If it fails or goes stale, our team is alerted."},"2689":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-19","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#how-we-protect-its-reputation","content":"**Full authentication alignment** — the relay signs with DKIM for your verified domain, `include:_spf.north-pipe.ca` covers SPF for IPv4 and IPv6, and both align with DMARC. See DNS Setup."},"2690":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-20","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#what-changes-between-tiers","content":"Plans differ in limits and features, not in where your mail comes from:"},"2691":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-21","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#what-changes-between-tiers","content":"| Tier     | Price (CAD/mo) | Emails/Month | Custom domains | Inbox cap | Inbox retention | Features                            |\n| -------- | -------------- | ------------ | -------------- | --------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Free** | $0             | 3,000        | --             | --        | --              | API sending from a system subdomain |","table":"table-1"},"2692":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-22","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#what-changes-between-tiers","content":"| Tier        | Price (CAD/mo) | Emails/Month | Custom domains | Inbox cap | Inbox retention | Features                                  |\n| ----------- | -------------- | ------------ | -------------- | --------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| **Starter** | $5             | 5,000        | 1              | 1 GB      | 90 d            | + Inbox (JMAP + IMAP), aliases, 1 webhook |","table":"table-1"},"2693":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-23","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#what-changes-between-tiers","content":"| Tier      | Price (CAD/mo) | Emails/Month | Custom domains | Inbox cap | Inbox retention | Features                           |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------ | -------------- | --------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| **Micro** | $12            | 20,000       | 2              | 2 GB      | 180 d           | + Campaigns, templates, scheduling |","table":"table-1"},"2694":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-24","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#what-changes-between-tiers","content":"| Tier    | Price (CAD/mo) | Emails/Month | Custom domains | Inbox cap | Inbox retention | Features                                    |\n| ------- | -------------- | ------------ | -------------- | --------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| **Pro** | $29            | 50,000       | 5              | 5 GB      | 365 d           | + Catch-all, team members, priority support |","table":"table-1"},"2695":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-25","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#what-changes-between-tiers","content":"| Tier      | Price (CAD/mo) | Emails/Month | Custom domains | Inbox cap | Inbox retention | Features    |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------ | -------------- | --------- | --------------- | ----------- |\n| **Scale** | $79            | 150,000      | 20             | 20 GB     | 365 d           | High volume |","table":"table-1"},"2696":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-26","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#what-changes-between-tiers","content":"See Plans & Pricing for the full comparison."},"2697":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-27","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#upgrading","content":"Upgrades take effect immediately:"},"2698":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-28","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#upgrading","content":"Go to **Dashboard → Settings → Billing**"},"2699":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-29","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#upgrading","content":"Select your new tier"},"2700":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-30","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#upgrading","content":"Complete payment"},"2701":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-31","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#upgrading","content":"Your new quota and features apply to your next message. An upgrade never requires code changes, new credentials or DNS changes — your SMTP settings, API keys and SPF/DKIM records stay exactly as they are."},"2702":{"id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system-32","page_id":"/docs/features/two-pool-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/two-pool-system#previously-the-two-pool-system","content":"Until September 2026, NorthRelay routed Free/Starter/Micro accounts through a \"Shared\" IP and Pro/Scale accounts through an \"Isolated\" IP. That design was retired in favour of one well-protected IP for everyone: a single warm, monitored relay with a strict sender policy is simpler, easier to defend and delivers at least as well as splitting traffic across two addresses. This page keeps its URL so existing links continue to work."},"2703":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","type":"page","content":"Send Your First Email","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-email"},"2704":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","content":"A step-by-step guide to sending your first email through NorthRelay"},"2705":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-email#send-your-first-email","content":"Send Your First Email"},"2706":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-email#using-smtp","content":"Using SMTP"},"2707":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-email#nodejs-with-nodemailer","content":"Node.js with Nodemailer"},"2708":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-email#python-with-smtplib","content":"Python with smtplib"},"2709":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-email","type":"heading","tags":[],"url