url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#diagnosis","content":"Diagnosis"},"3809":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-20","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#fix-unblock-an-ip","content":"Fix: Unblock an IP"},"3810":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-21","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#prevention","content":"Prevention"},"3811":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-22","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#sql-directory-queries","content":"SQL Directory Queries"},"3812":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-23","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"Query Types"},"3813":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-24","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#managing-sql-queries","content":"Managing SQL Queries"},"3814":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-25","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#catch-all-support","content":"Catch-All Support"},"3815":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-26","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-management","content":"Principal Management"},"3816":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-27","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#creating-a-principal","content":"Creating a Principal"},"3817":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-28","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"Principal Fields"},"3818":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-29","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Outbound routing"},"3819":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-30","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Next Steps"},"3820":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-31","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#stalwart-mail-server-setup","content":"> Configure Stalwart's split-role architecture for outbound relay and inbound mailbox."},"3821":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-32","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#current-hosted-mailbox-deployment","content":"The hosted mailbox service runs Stalwart Community 0.16.23 on the former shared\nrelay host, with native JMAP administration. Client access is documented in\nHosted email access. The deployment source is the\nplatform repository's `infra/mailbox-next` directory."},"3822":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-33","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#current-hosted-mailbox-deployment","content":"The generic split-role examples below also describe the separately versioned\napplication sending instance. Do not apply an old SQL-directory configuration\nor `/api/principal` management example to the 0.16 production mailbox. Mailbox\nadministration uses native `x:Account/*`, `x:Domain/*` and `x:AppPassword/*` methods."},"3823":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"Stalwart Mail Server is a modern, Rust-based mail server distributed as a single binary. It supports SMTP, IMAP, JMAP, and includes built-in spam filtering, DKIM, and a management API."},"3824":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"NorthRelay uses Stalwart in a **split-role architecture** with two separate instances:"},"3825":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"| Instance           | Role            | Location      | Purpose                                                              |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Outbound Relay** | Queue + routing | Sanctuary VPS | Accepts SMTP submissions, routes to the sending relay, manages queue |","table":"table-0"},"3826":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-37","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"| Instance            | Role        | Location    | Purpose                                                |\n| ------------------- | ----------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Inbound Mailbox** | IMAP + JMAP | Mailbox VPS | Receives inbound mail, user mailboxes, dashboard inbox |","table":"table-0"},"3827":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-38","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"These are independent Stalwart instances with separate configurations, separate admin tokens, and separate Management APIs."},"3828":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-39","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"The relay instance handles all outbound email:"},"3829":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-40","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Key characteristics:"},"3830":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-41","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Runs on the Sanctuary VPS alongside the dashboard"},"3831":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-42","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Uses host networking in Docker for SMTP port binding"},"3832":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-43","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Routes every email, on every tier, to the single sending relay (`sovereign.north-pipe.ca`)"},"3833":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"DKIM signing is **disabled** (handled by OpenDKIM on relay VPSes)"},"3834":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Management API on port 8080 (internal only)"},"3835":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"The mailbox instance handles all inbound email and user inbox access:"},"3836":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Key characteristics:"},"3837":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Runs on a dedicated Mailbox VPS"},"3838":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-49","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"MX records point here (`mx.northrelay.ca`)"},"3839":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-50","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Provides IMAP and JMAP access for dashboard inbox"},"3840":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-51","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Uses SQL directory queries against PostgreSQL for authentication"},"3841":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-52","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Each user's inbox email = their subdomain slot email"},"3842":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-53","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#toml-configuration-basics","content":"Stalwart's static configuration uses TOML format. Key sections:"},"3843":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-54","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#authentication","content":"The `fallback-admin.secret` is the token used for Management API and CLI authentication."},"3844":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-55","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#queue-and-routing","content":"See Outbound routing below for the details."},"3845":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-56","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#management-api","content":"The Management API runs on port 8080 and provides HTTP endpoints for administration."},"3846":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-57","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#authentication-1","content":"All API requests require authentication:"},"3847":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-58","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#cli-tool","content":"The Stalwart CLI (`stalwart-cli`) manages runtime configuration stored in RocksDB."},"3848":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-59","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#ip-blocking-prevention","content":"> **This is the most common operational issue with Stalwart.**"},"3849":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-60","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#ip-blocking-prevention","content":"Stalwart has an auto-ban feature that blocks IP addresses after failed authentication attempts. Blocked IPs are stored in **RocksDB** (not the TOML config), so they persist across restarts."},"3850":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-61","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"SMTP connection closes immediately without a banner"},"3851":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-62","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"Telnet to port 25 connects then disconnects instantly"},"3852":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-63","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"No error in application logs - the connection is dropped at the Stalwart level"},"3853":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-64","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#prevention","content":"Add trusted IPs to the allowlist in your TOML config:"},"3854":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-65","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#prevention","content":"Or disable auto-ban entirely for development:"},"3855":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-66","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#sql-directory-queries","content":"The mailbox Stalwart instance uses SQL queries against PostgreSQL for user authentication and mail routing. These queries are stored in RocksDB and queried at runtime."},"3856":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-67","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query        | Purpose                                    | Supports Catch-All |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------ |\n| `recipients` | Determine if an address should be accepted | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3857":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-68","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query  | Purpose                                | Supports Catch-All |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `name` | Resolve a user account from an address | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3858":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-69","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query    | Purpose                                     | Supports Catch-All |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `emails` | Get all allowed sender addresses for a user | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3859":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-70","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query     | Purpose                              | Supports Catch-All |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------ |\n| `secrets` | Get password hash for authentication | No                 |","table":"table-1"},"3860":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-71","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query     | Purpose                 | Supports Catch-All |\n| --------- | ----------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `members` | Group membership lookup | No                 |","table":"table-1"},"3861":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-72","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#catch-all-support","content":"The `recipients` and `name` queries include catch-all logic: if no exact match is found, they check whether the domain has `is_inbox_hosted = true` in the `domains` table. If so, all mail to that domain routes to the domain owner."},"3862":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-73","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-management","content":"Stalwart principals represent user accounts. For the mailbox instance, principals are provisioned automatically during user registration."},"3863":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-74","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field  | Description                    |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ |\n| `type` | `individual` for user accounts |","table":"table-2"},"3864":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-75","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field  | Description                        |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `name` | Primary identifier (usually email) |","table":"table-2"},"3865":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-76","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field    | Description                                                     |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emails` | Array of all email addresses this principal can send/receive as |","table":"table-2"},"3866":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-77","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field     | Description                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `secrets` | Array containing bcrypt password hash |","table":"table-2"},"3867":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-78","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field   | Description                                 |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `quota` | Mailbox size limit in bytes (0 = unlimited) |","table":"table-2"},"3868":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-79","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"The outbound relay sends every message, on every tier, through one route to the sending relay:"},"3869":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-80","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"| Route   | Address                                                   | Relay VPS      |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `relay` | `sovereign.north-pipe.ca:25` (over WireGuard, `10.0.2.2`) | `76.13.27.101` |","table":"table-3"},"3870":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-81","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Rules that matter in Stalwart v0.15:"},"3871":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-82","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"The route address **must be a DNS hostname**, never a raw IP — a raw IP triggers a \"record not found for MX\" error. On Sanctuary, `/etc/hosts` maps `sovereign.north-pipe.ca` to the WireGuard address `10.0.2.2` so the route stays inside the tunnel."},"3872":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-83","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"`queue.outbound.next-hop` is ignored; only `queue.strategy.route` selects the route."},"3873":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-84","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"RocksDB keys override the TOML file. After changing the route, delete any stale `queue.strategy.route` / `queue.route.*` keys and run `server reload-config`."},"3874":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-85","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Never set `queue.outbound.is_local` on the relay instance — it has no mailboxes."},"3875":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-86","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Tier does not affect routing. See Sending Infrastructure for what protects the relay's reputation."},"3876":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-87","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Configuration Guide - Environment variables and service configuration"},"3877":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-88","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Monitoring - Health checks for Stalwart and related services"},"3878":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-89","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Runbooks - Troubleshooting Stalwart issues"},"3879":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"page","content":"MCP Server","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","SDKs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server"},"3880":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-0","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","content":"NorthRelay MCP Server for AI agent integration with Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Codex, Cursor, Windsurf, and other MCP-compatible clients"},"3881":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-1","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#mcp-server","content":"MCP Server"},"3882":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-2","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"What is MCP?"},"3883":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-3","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#installation","content":"Installation"},"3884":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-4","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"3885":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-5","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#environment-variables","content":"Environment Variables"},"3886":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-6","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-code","content":"Claude Code"},"3887":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-7","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#codex","content":"Codex"},"3888":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-8","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"Claude Desktop"},"3889":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-9","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#cursor","content":"Cursor"},"3890":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-10","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#windsurf","content":"Windsurf"},"3891":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-11","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-mode","content":"Hosted mode"},"3892":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-12","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#connector-mode","content":"Connector mode"},"3893":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-13","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#tool-groups","content":"Tool Groups"},"3894":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-14","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#usage-examples","content":"Usage Examples"},"3895":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-15","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#sending-emails","content":"Sending Emails"},"3896":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-16","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#managing-templates","content":"Managing Templates"},"3897":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-17","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#checking-delivery-status","content":"Checking Delivery Status"},"3898":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-18","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#deliverability-checks","content":"Deliverability Checks"},"3899":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-19","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#campaign-management","content":"Campaign Management"},"3900":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-20","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#mailing-lists-and-subscriptions","content":"Mailing Lists and Subscriptions"},"3901":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-21","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"3902":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-22","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#server-not-starting","content":"Server Not Starting"},"3903":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-23","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#tools-not-appearing-in-ai-client","content":"Tools Not Appearing in AI Client"},"3904":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-24","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#authentication-errors","content":"Authentication Errors"},"3905":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-25","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"Hosted Endpoint Connects But Shows No Tools"},"3906":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-26","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#related","content":"Related"},"3907":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-27","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#mcp-server","content":"The NorthRelay MCP Server (`@northrelay/mcp-server` 1.9.0) exposes the full NorthRelay API as tools that AI agents can use directly. It implements the Model Context Protocol (MCP) standard, allowing AI assistants to send emails, manage templates, check delivery status, and more through natural language."},"3908":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-28","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open standard that lets AI applications interact with external services through structured tool calls. Instead of writing code, you describe what you want in plain language, and the AI agent calls the appropriate NorthRelay tools on your behalf."},"3909":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-29","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"**Supported AI clients:**"},"3910":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-30","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"Claude Code"},"3911":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-31","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"Claude Desktop"},"3912":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-32","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"Codex (CLI, IDE extension and desktop app)"},"3913":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-33","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"Cursor"},"3914":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-34","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"Windsurf"},"3915":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-35","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"Any MCP-compatible client"},"3916":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-36","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#what-is-mcp","content":"The server runs in one of two modes. Over **stdio** the client starts it\nlocally and gives it your NorthRelay API key. In **hosted (HTTP)** mode one\nrunning instance serves a team over the network, callers present a bearer\ntoken, and the API key stays on the host. See Hosted mode."},"3917":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-37","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#installation","content":"No separate installation is needed. The server runs via `npx`:"},"3918":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-38","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#installation","content":"Or install globally:"},"3919":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-39","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#environment-variables","content":"| Variable             | Required | Default | Description             |\n| -------------------- | -------- | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| `NORTHRELAY_API_KEY` | Yes      | —       | Your NorthRelay API key |","table":"table-0"},"3920":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-40","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#environment-variables","content":"| Variable              | Required | Default                     | Description         |\n| --------------------- | -------- | --------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `NORTHRELAY_BASE_URL` | No       | `https://app.northrelay.ca` | Custom API base URL |","table":"table-0"},"3921":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-41","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#environment-variables","content":"| Variable                    | Required         | Default | Description                                                                          |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `NORTHRELAY_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` | Hosted mode only | —       | Bearer token(s) callers must present; comma-separate several to rotate without a gap |","table":"table-0"},"3922":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-42","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#environment-variables","content":"| Variable              | Required | Default | Description                          |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `NORTHRELAY_MCP_PORT` | No       | `3010`  | Port for hosted mode (`--port` wins) |","table":"table-0"},"3923":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-43","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#environment-variables","content":"| Variable              | Required | Default     | Description                               |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `NORTHRELAY_MCP_BIND` | No       | `127.0.0.1` | Interface for hosted mode (`--bind` wins) |","table":"table-0"},"3924":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-44","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#environment-variables","content":"| Variable                        | Required | Default  | Description                                |\n| ------------------------------- | -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `NORTHRELAY_MCP_SESSION_TTL_MS` | No       | `600000` | Close a hosted session left idle this long |","table":"table-0"},"3925":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-45","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#environment-variables","content":"Keep the API key and the bearer token out of files you commit or text you\npaste. Where a client can read a secret from the environment, the examples\nbelow do that."},"3926":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-46","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-code","content":"Over stdio, with the API key passed through `--env`:"},"3927":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-47","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-code","content":"Against a hosted endpoint, with the bearer as a header (`--scope user` makes\nit available in every project):"},"3928":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-48","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-code","content":"In a project's checked-in `.mcp.json`, write the placeholder and Claude Code\nexpands it from the environment when it loads:"},"3929":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-49","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-code","content":"`claude mcp list`, or `/mcp` inside a session, shows whether it connected."},"3930":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-50","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#codex","content":"The Codex CLI, IDE extension and desktop app share `~/.codex/config.toml`\n(or a project's `.codex/config.toml`)."},"3931":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-51","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#codex","content":"Over stdio:"},"3932":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-52","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#codex","content":"which writes:"},"3933":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-53","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#codex","content":"Against a hosted endpoint, name the environment variable that holds the\nbearer — the file itself never contains it:"},"3934":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-54","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"Add the following to your Claude Desktop configuration file:"},"3935":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-55","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"**macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`\n**Windows:** `%APPDATA%\\Claude\\claude_desktop_config.json`\n**Linux:** `~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`"},"3936":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-56","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"Restart Claude Desktop after saving the configuration."},"3937":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-57","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"**claude.ai and Claude Desktop custom connectors.** The *Add custom\nconnector* dialog reaches a remote MCP server and authenticates by OAuth —\nthere is no field for a bearer token. A hosted instance running in\nconnector mode is what it needs:"},"3938":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-58","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"Settings → Connectors → *Add custom connector*, with the endpoint URL\n(`https://mcp.example.net/mcp`), no client id and no secret."},"3939":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-59","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"A NorthRelay sign-in page opens. It names the client that is asking and\nthe address the token will be sent to, and starts from read-only\npermissions; tick exactly what the connector should be able to do."},"3940":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-60","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"Approving issues an API key named `oauth-<client>-…`. It appears under\n**Settings → API Keys**, expires after 30 days (the connector renews it\nitself), and revoking it there ends the connector's access."},"3941":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-61","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#claude-desktop","content":"A hosted instance that serves only a shared token cannot be added as a\nconnector; use Claude Code or Codex for that one."},"3942":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-62","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#cursor","content":"In Cursor settings, add an MCP server with:"},"3943":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-63","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#cursor","content":"**Name:** `northrelay`"},"3944":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-64","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#cursor","content":"**Command:** `npx @northrelay/mcp-server`"},"3945":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-65","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#cursor","content":"**Environment:** `NORTHRELAY_API_KEY=nr_live_your_api_key_here`"},"3946":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-66","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#windsurf","content":"Add to your Windsurf MCP configuration:"},"3947":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-67","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-mode","content":"By default the server speaks stdio and each client spawns its own copy. Pass\n`--http` to serve Streamable HTTP instead, so a team, a CI job, or an agent\nrunning elsewhere can share one instance without holding the API key:"},"3948":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-68","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-mode","content":"The MCP endpoint is `/mcp`; `GET /healthz` is an unauthenticated probe."},"3949":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-69","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-mode","content":"A bearer token is **required**. The endpoint can send real mail, rewrite\ntemplates and clear suppressions, so the server refuses to start without\n`NORTHRELAY_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` and answers `401` to a wrong one. Every caller\npresents `Authorization: Bearer <token>`."},"3950":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-70","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-mode","content":"It binds `127.0.0.1` by default. Put it behind a reverse proxy that\nterminates TLS rather than exposing the port directly."},"3951":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-71","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-mode","content":"A session idle past `NORTHRELAY_MCP_SESSION_TTL_MS` is closed, so a client\nthat crashes without ending its session is not held forever."},"3952":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-72","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-mode","content":"To check an endpoint from a client machine:"},"3953":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-73","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#connector-mode","content":"Set `NORTHRELAY_MCP_PUBLIC_URL` to the origin the instance is reached at,\nand a caller may present its **own** NorthRelay API key as the bearer\ninstead of the shared token:"},"3954":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-74","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#connector-mode","content":"Each session then acts as the key it presented — scoped and revocable in\nthat account's key list — and the process needs no `NORTHRELAY_API_KEY` of\nits own unless it also serves a shared token. The server publishes\n`/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` naming the NorthRelay platform as\nits authorization server, which is how the claude.ai and Claude Desktop\nconnectors find their way to the sign-in page. A key is checked with the\nplatform once, when a session opens; a revoked key is refused at the next\nsession."},"3955":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-75","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#connector-mode","content":"| Variable                    | Description                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `NORTHRELAY_MCP_PUBLIC_URL` | This endpoint's public origin, `https://` (or `http://localhost` for a local instance), no path |","table":"table-1"},"3956":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-76","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#connector-mode","content":"The platform side needs nothing configured: every NorthRelay account can\napprove connectors, and `OAUTH_CONNECTORS_DISABLED=true` on the platform\nswitches the authorization server off."},"3957":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-77","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#tool-groups","content":"The MCP server (1.7.0) exposes 149 tools in 21 groups."},"3958":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-78","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#tool-groups","content":"| Group      | Tools                            | Description                             |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| **emails** | `send_email`, `get_email_events` | Send email and read its delivery events |","table":"table-2"},"3959":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-79","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#tool-groups","content":"| Group                      | Tools                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        