/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#tools-not-appearing-in-ai-client","content":"Restart your AI client after updating the configuration"},"4007":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-127","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#tools-not-appearing-in-ai-client","content":"Verify the configuration file path is correct for your OS"},"4008":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-128","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#tools-not-appearing-in-ai-client","content":"Check that `npx` is available in your system PATH"},"4009":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-129","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#authentication-errors","content":"Ensure your API key:"},"4010":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-130","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#authentication-errors","content":"Starts with `nr_live_` (production) or `nr_test_` (testing)"},"4011":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-131","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#authentication-errors","content":"Has not been revoked"},"4012":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-132","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#authentication-errors","content":"Has the necessary permissions for the operations you are performing — a\nkey missing a scope answers `403 SCOPE_INSUFFICIENT` naming the scope"},"4013":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-133","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"The client presented the wrong bearer: the server answers `401`, which most\nclients report as a failed connection. Check the token the client was given\nagainst `NORTHRELAY_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` on the host."},"4014":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-134","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"The client was pointed at the host root instead of `/mcp`."},"4015":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-135","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"Adding it as a claude.ai custom connector without `NORTHRELAY_MCP_PUBLIC_URL`\nset on the instance: that dialog cannot send a bearer token, so the\ninstance has to run in connector mode."},"4016":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-136","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"The connector reports \"Couldn't register with … sign-in service\", or\nconnects but never offers to sign in: the instance's\n`/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` is not reachable through the\nreverse proxy, or names a platform origin the client cannot reach.\n`curl -s https://mcp.example.net/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`\nshould answer with `authorization_servers`. A proxy that forwards only\n`/mcp` and `/healthz` has to forward that path too — the instance answers\nboth the bare path and the `/mcp`-suffixed form, so with Caddy:"},"4017":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-137","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#related","content":"TypeScript SDK for programmatic Node.js integration"},"4018":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-138","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#related","content":"Python SDK for programmatic Python integration"},"4019":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-139","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#related","content":"API Reference for raw HTTP API details"},"4020":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","type":"page","content":"Python SDK","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documen