                        | Endpoint                                          | Returns                    |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `subscriptions.resend_confirmation(email)` | `POST /subscriptions/{email}/resend-confirmation` | `ResendConfirmationResult` |","table":"table-1"},"4057":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-36","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#subscriptions","content":"`consent` takes a dict (`ip`, `user_agent` or `userAgent`, `text`) or a `Consent` model. Emails are URL-encoded in paths for you. `unsubscribe` raises `ValueError` when `scope=\"list\"` has no `list_id` or `scope=\"topic\"` has no `topic_id`; `update_preferences` raises `ValueError` when none of `topics`, `lists` or `unsubscribe_all=True` is given. Subscription writes are not retried automatically."},"4058":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-37","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#contacts","content":"`contacts.create()` does not record consent or fire webhooks; use `subscriptions.subscribe()` when a person signs up. `bulk_upsert` creates new contacts and skips existing ones; it does not update them."},"4059":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-38","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                        | Endpoint              |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `contacts.list_lists(*, page, limit, type, search, archived)` | `GET /contacts/lists` |","table":"table-2"},"4060":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-39","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                                                                         | Endpoint          |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `contacts.get_list(id)` / `create_list(name, description, *, type, topic_id, tracking_enabled, segment_rules)` | `/contacts/lists` |","table":"table-2"},"4061":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-40","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                                                    | Endpoint                                                       |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.update_list(id, name, description, *, topic_id, tracking_enabled, is_archived)` | `PATCH /contacts/lists/{id}` (`topic_id=None` removes the tag) |","table":"table-2"},"4062":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-41","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                     | Endpoint                                 |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.delete_list(id)` | `DELETE /contacts/lists/{id}` (archives) |","table":"table-2"},"4063":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-42","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                                         | Endpoint                           |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.list_members(id, *, page, limit, filter)` (alias `get_list_members`) | `GET /contacts/lists/{id}/members` |","table":"table-2"},"4064":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-43","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                                  | Endpoint                            |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.add_to_list(id, contact_ids=None, *, emails, create_missing)` | `POST /contacts/lists/{id}/members` |","table":"table-2"},"4065":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-44","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                       | Endpoint                              |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.remove_from_list(id, contact_ids=None, *, emails)` | `DELETE /contacts/lists/{id}/members` |","table":"table-2"},"4066":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-45","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"`remove_from_list` is the list owner removing someone (the membership is deleted). To record that a recipient asked to leave, use `subscriptions.unsubscribe(email, scope=\"list\", list_id=...)`."},"4067":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-46","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#csv-import","content":"When `mappings` is omitted, columns named like email, first name, last name and phone are mapped automatically. `file_name` sets the upload name when you pass bytes."},"4068":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-47","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#topics-suppression-groups","content":"`client.topics` is an alias of `client.suppression_groups`. A topic member is an address that **opted out** of that topic. Topic methods return the API response as a dict."},"4069":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-48","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#topics-suppression-groups","content":"The member methods only edit the opt-out rows. For a recipient's own choice, prefer `subscriptions.unsubscribe(..., scope=\"topic\")` or `update_preferences`, which also update tagged lists and fire webhooks."},"4070":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-49","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#signup-forms","content":"Form methods return the `data` object of the API response as a dict."},"4071":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-50","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#signup-forms","content":"`forms.submit(form_id, values)` posts answers keyed by `fieldKey` to a published form. From your own backend, `subscriptions.subscribe()` is usually the better choice."},"4072":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-51","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#webhooks","content":"`WEBHOOK_EVENT_TYPES` lists every event name the API accepts."},"4073":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-52","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#suppressions","content":"Emails are URL-encoded in paths for you. `reason` is one of `Bounce`, `Complaint`, `Unsubscribe` or `Manual`. To record a recipient's own opt-out, prefer `subscriptions.unsubscribe()`."},"4074":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-53","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#templates-and-brands-studio","content":"Every template is a Studio design. Dashboard templates use the application key `\"account\"`; a product with an `nr_app_` credential uses its own key."},"4075":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-54","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#templates-and-brands-studio","content":"`templates` and `brand_theme` are deprecated (sunset 30 April 2027). Template ids are design ids, so sending with `template_id` keeps working."},"4076":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-55","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#other-resources","content":"| Attribute | Methods          